1
00:01:07,652 --> 00:01:08,653
Damn it.

2
00:01:44,731 --> 00:01:45,982
Stay back!

3
00:02:26,022 --> 00:02:28,482
Outlaw 1, flight of two,
checking in as fragged.

4
00:02:28,483 --> 00:02:31,735
Red Hook 3507,
tally two hostile, one o'clock.

5
00:02:31,736 --> 00:02:33,988
So I got Anderton's daughter
one of those Cabbage Patch dolls

6
00:02:33,989 --> 00:02:35,072
for her birthday.

7
00:02:35,073 --> 00:02:36,615
Can someone explain them to me?

8
00:02:36,616 --> 00:02:39,535
- What do you mean?
- Their faces. Why do they look like that?

9
00:02:39,536 --> 00:02:41,787
Their eyes are too small
and their cheeks are all swollen,

10
00:02:41,788 --> 00:02:43,164
it's like they're on steroids.

11
00:02:47,252 --> 00:02:50,337
I think they're kinda cute.
They're just chubby like babies.

12
00:02:50,338 --> 00:02:53,048
You know, if I saw a baby like that
I'd never stop screaming.

13
00:02:53,049 --> 00:02:56,886
Outlaw 2, tally. My understanding is
they're born in a cabbage patch.

14
00:02:56,887 --> 00:02:58,721
You say that like it's not insane.

15
00:02:58,722 --> 00:03:00,640
Whatever happened to
good ole Raggedy Andy?

16
00:03:01,391 --> 00:03:03,642
- Are we gonna do this drill or not?
- Uh-oh.

17
00:03:03,643 --> 00:03:04,810
Russians are getting impatient.

18
00:03:04,811 --> 00:03:07,605
Engaging north man. Tapes on. Fight's on.

19
00:03:07,606 --> 00:03:10,108
Outlaw 2, taking south man.
Turning and burning.

20
00:03:20,744 --> 00:03:21,912
What you gonna do?

21
00:03:33,757 --> 00:03:36,051
Hey, you got nowhere to go, boss.
You ready to call it?

22
00:03:37,093 --> 00:03:38,428
Uh-huh. Maybe.

23
00:03:46,436 --> 00:03:48,437
Kill north man. You're dead, Nikita.

24
00:03:48,438 --> 00:03:50,439
- Dang it!
- Splash one Mig.

25
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,857
Longshot, say status.

26
00:03:51,858 --> 00:03:53,234
South man is a kill, bubba.

27
00:03:53,235 --> 00:03:55,569
I think we can all agree
that this was deeply embarrassing

28
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:56,946
for our Soviet colleagues.

29
00:03:56,947 --> 00:03:58,948
Hey, you got lucky, Lieutenant.

30
00:03:58,949 --> 00:04:00,242
I'll see ya on the boat.

31
00:04:04,287 --> 00:04:07,666
Assassin, I seem to be having
a flight controls malfunction.

32
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,542
What's going on?

33
00:04:10,043 --> 00:04:13,128
Right aileron's jammed.
I'm holding a full left stick.

34
00:04:13,129 --> 00:04:16,298
Okay, just… Hey, hold her steady.
Lemme get a visual.

35
00:04:18,593 --> 00:04:19,843
Oh, yeah, I see it.

36
00:04:19,844 --> 00:04:22,179
Can't land on mom if
I'm shaking like this.

37
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:25,182
- LSO, you copy?
- LSO copies.

38
00:04:25,183 --> 00:04:27,977
All right. Get my boys on the boat.
I'm gonna hang back with Boomer.

39
00:04:27,978 --> 00:04:28,979
Good luck, brother.

40
00:04:32,315 --> 00:04:34,441
- Damn it.
- Unpucker, Boomer.

41
00:04:34,442 --> 00:04:36,026
Let's get you up to altitude.

42
00:04:36,027 --> 00:04:38,613
No-go. Juice is 2.1. I'm nearly dry.

43
00:04:39,364 --> 00:04:40,447
Think I gotta punch out.

44
00:04:40,448 --> 00:04:42,575
No. Let's think of the taxpayers.

45
00:04:42,576 --> 00:04:44,368
I'm gonna try something. I just…

46
00:04:44,369 --> 00:04:46,453
I want you to hold her
as steady as you can.

47
00:04:46,454 --> 00:04:47,914
What the hell are you doing?

48
00:04:48,540 --> 00:04:50,750
- I'm gonna unjam your aileron.
- How?

49
00:04:51,334 --> 00:04:54,212
Don't worry.
Just drop your gear, fly your needles.

50
00:04:59,467 --> 00:05:01,093
It's too unstable.

51
00:05:01,094 --> 00:05:03,221
I know. This is kind of crazy.
Just go with me.

52
00:05:05,849 --> 00:05:07,350
You're gonna get us both killed.

53
00:05:19,654 --> 00:05:22,156
Oh, shit. Come on!

54
00:05:22,157 --> 00:05:24,700
It's okay. That's all right.
I'm a professional.

55
00:05:24,701 --> 00:05:26,243
It's no-go.

56
00:05:26,244 --> 00:05:28,704
Wave off, 382. You're gonna hit the tower.

57
00:05:28,705 --> 00:05:30,122
He's right. You gotta abort.

58
00:05:30,123 --> 00:05:32,833
You just focus on Meatball. Lineup AOA.

59
00:05:32,834 --> 00:05:35,086
Now, you're gonna feel a little pressure.

60
00:05:49,976 --> 00:05:52,686
Okay, all right. I owe you one, buddy.

61
00:05:52,687 --> 00:05:53,896
I owe you more.

62
00:05:53,897 --> 00:05:55,356
You just made me employee of the month.

63
00:05:55,357 --> 00:05:58,068
They're gonna let me
park my plane next to the entrance.

64
00:05:58,568 --> 00:06:00,653
Let me say to the hostage families,

65
00:06:00,654 --> 00:06:01,737
we have not given up.

66
00:06:01,738 --> 00:06:02,988
We never will.

67
00:06:02,989 --> 00:06:05,699
And I promise you we'll use
every legitimate means

68
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:09,453
to free your loved ones from captivity.
But I must also…

69
00:06:09,454 --> 00:06:12,539
- Hey, what'd he say?
- He said I'm gonna live another 75 years.

70
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:15,168
Oh, come on. Look, is that new stuff
he's got you on doing anything?

71
00:06:15,669 --> 00:06:17,294
I told you I'm cured.

72
00:06:17,295 --> 00:06:18,463
- Oh, you're cured?
- Excuse me?

73
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:22,007
Rules are you gotta be in a wheelchair
until you leave the hospital.

74
00:06:22,008 --> 00:06:24,635
- Really?
- Come on. No, no, no. Let's not make a--

75
00:06:24,636 --> 00:06:27,096
Dad, you don't have to protect me
from this stuff.

76
00:06:27,097 --> 00:06:28,973
I'm pretty good with stressful things.

77
00:06:28,974 --> 00:06:32,476
Oh, Lord.
Well, they're gonna try a new medicine.

78
00:06:32,477 --> 00:06:34,437
It's worked on rats,
so it should be good for me.

79
00:06:36,982 --> 00:06:39,650
Hey, you wanna go to the Turf tonight?
Grab a steak or something?

80
00:06:39,651 --> 00:06:42,444
- I thought you were meetin' your friends?
- You're my friends.

81
00:06:42,445 --> 00:06:43,947
Well, thank you very much.

82
00:06:44,781 --> 00:06:48,284
But if you wanna cheer me up,
then go drink with your pals.

83
00:06:48,285 --> 00:06:50,912
At least pretend you haven't
given up so much for me.

84
00:06:51,746 --> 00:06:55,541
Besides,
I'm going out with that girl tonight.

85
00:06:55,542 --> 00:06:56,709
Oh, nice.

86
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:58,002
Dinner and a funeral.

87
00:06:58,003 --> 00:06:59,128
You're a dick.

88
00:06:59,129 --> 00:07:01,339
GASLAMP QUARTER

89
00:07:03,383 --> 00:07:05,593
Oh, please. Don't let Gorbachev fool you.

90
00:07:05,594 --> 00:07:08,178
Right, well, I don't know if
Gorbachev is the problem.

91
00:07:08,179 --> 00:07:09,597
- It seems to me like…
- Oh, no.

92
00:07:09,598 --> 00:07:12,433
- …he is trying to make some reforms.
- The guy came up through the Politburo.

93
00:07:12,434 --> 00:07:14,393
He's a dyed-in-the-wool Communist.

94
00:07:14,394 --> 00:07:16,729
- Regardless of what he calls himself.
- Here comes Captain America.

95
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:18,230
- That's right.
- Honestly. I don't see

96
00:07:18,231 --> 00:07:20,357
the big difference between
capitalism and communism.

97
00:07:20,358 --> 00:07:22,902
- You what? The whole Soviet system…
- Why would you poke the bear, man?

98
00:07:22,903 --> 00:07:25,237
- …flies in the face of human nature.
- Great, now he's not gonna shut up.

99
00:07:25,238 --> 00:07:26,947
You can't reform something

100
00:07:26,948 --> 00:07:29,033
- that's fundamentally broken.
- I didn't sign up for this course.

101
00:07:29,034 --> 00:07:31,201
- No, you didn't.
- You didn't sign up for this course.

102
00:07:31,202 --> 00:07:33,495
- Lenin, Stalin, you know…
- Didn't we just go out?

103
00:07:33,496 --> 00:07:36,040
These guys would pretend that
we're living in some-- Hi, there.

104
00:07:36,041 --> 00:07:38,792
We're living in some,
you know, big, happy collective.

105
00:07:38,793 --> 00:07:42,296
You know, but for some reason,
that collective is always at the cost of

106
00:07:42,297 --> 00:07:43,797
individual freedoms.

107
00:07:43,798 --> 00:07:46,884
- Watch out!
- Sorry. Hi. You drive safe tonight, sir.

108
00:07:46,885 --> 00:07:48,135
Okay. Take me, for example.

109
00:07:48,136 --> 00:07:51,181
I think we can all agree
that I'm the best pilot in the 3rd Fleet.

110
00:07:51,890 --> 00:07:53,474
Boomer, I know you can.

111
00:07:53,475 --> 00:07:55,768
- What? Wh… No shame, this guy!
- Save me, Troy.

112
00:07:55,769 --> 00:07:58,520
- I don't have any shame. Nor should I.
- Save me.

113
00:07:58,521 --> 00:08:00,648
Right, because in America,
we celebrate being the best.

114
00:08:00,649 --> 00:08:02,316
- Yep.
- We reward greatness.

115
00:08:02,317 --> 00:08:04,235
You know what happens
over there if you're great?

116
00:08:04,236 --> 00:08:05,402
What's that? Tell them.

117
00:08:05,403 --> 00:08:07,738
Nothing. You're just another comrade.

118
00:08:07,739 --> 00:08:09,907
- That's not a society…
- You guys sucking up to him?

119
00:08:09,908 --> 00:08:11,200
- …that's a prison.
- What?

120
00:08:11,201 --> 00:08:14,245
And anyone who doesn't fight to break out
of that, well, then they're, you know…

121
00:08:14,246 --> 00:08:15,704
- They're part of the problem.
- Anyone?

122
00:08:15,705 --> 00:08:17,623
Even the poor civs
who just happen to be born there?

123
00:08:17,624 --> 00:08:19,333
Silence is complicity.

124
00:08:19,334 --> 00:08:21,711
- Top guns! Yeah. What's up?
- Hey, buddy.

125
00:08:22,879 --> 00:08:25,506
You know, it's times like this
I am so glad they made that movie.

126
00:08:25,507 --> 00:08:27,342
- Uh-huh. What's up?
- Gentlemen.

127
00:08:28,552 --> 00:08:29,719
Commander.

128
00:08:30,512 --> 00:08:31,513
Everything okay, sir?

129
00:08:32,179 --> 00:08:33,974
Speak privately for a moment?

130
00:08:35,058 --> 00:08:36,268
Just Lieutenant Kelly.

131
00:08:37,519 --> 00:08:39,563
I've been briefed on your stunt today.

132
00:08:40,313 --> 00:08:42,648
Okay, yeah. I saw
an opportunity to help a wingman

133
00:08:42,649 --> 00:08:44,358
- and save an aircraft, so--
- Easy, Kelly.

134
00:08:44,359 --> 00:08:45,819
I'm not here to tear you down.

135
00:08:47,028 --> 00:08:48,405
You ever heard of Big Bird?

136
00:08:49,573 --> 00:08:51,408
Not the one from Sesame Street.

137
00:08:52,659 --> 00:08:53,660
Then no.

138
00:08:54,369 --> 00:08:55,662
Operation Big Bird.

139
00:08:56,371 --> 00:09:00,165
Since '71, the NRO has been
sending up recon satellites

140
00:09:00,166 --> 00:09:06,631
to keep track of what the Russians are
doing in the remote regions of USSR.

141
00:09:07,632 --> 00:09:10,009
Problem with that is
resolution is limited.

142
00:09:10,010 --> 00:09:13,305
So occasionally, we have to
send someone out for a closer look.

143
00:09:13,847 --> 00:09:14,931
You need a spy plane.

144
00:09:17,017 --> 00:09:18,518
You want me to fly a spy plane.

145
00:09:19,019 --> 00:09:22,396
You ship out to Ramstein Air Base
in Germany, 0400 tomorrow.

146
00:09:22,397 --> 00:09:23,439
I'll brief you there.

147
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:26,233
And it's TS,
so don't tell anyone you're leaving.

148
00:09:26,234 --> 00:09:28,402
Thank you, sir.
For the opportunity. Thank you.

149
00:09:28,403 --> 00:09:30,655
No, thank you. For earning it.

150
00:09:44,502 --> 00:09:46,754
Last week, we received imagery suggesting

151
00:09:46,755 --> 00:09:50,591
that the Russians are building
missile silos northeast of Nyandoma.

152
00:09:50,592 --> 00:09:55,095
That places our area of ops
1,200 miles inside the Soviet border.

153
00:09:55,096 --> 00:09:57,224
That's 30 minutes in and 30 minutes out.

154
00:09:58,016 --> 00:10:01,644
The site is flanked by four SAM sites
as far as we know.

155
00:10:01,645 --> 00:10:05,356
And the nearest Russian airstrip is
at Os'mino, 200 miles east.

156
00:10:05,357 --> 00:10:09,903
All this suggests that the Russians are
not using this site to make nesting dolls.

157
00:10:10,779 --> 00:10:14,114
You'll fly in at 80,000 feet,
above the SAM ceiling.

158
00:10:14,115 --> 00:10:16,076
You'll get your shots and you'll vámonos.

159
00:10:18,870 --> 00:10:20,330
You're the only one here, Kelly.

160
00:10:21,373 --> 00:10:22,957
You said 80,000 feet, sir.

161
00:10:22,958 --> 00:10:25,501
Doesn't that exceed
the max altitude of a U-2?

162
00:10:25,502 --> 00:10:28,463
That's correct.
But you won't be flying the U-2.

163
00:10:35,303 --> 00:10:37,763
The SR-71 Blackbird.

164
00:10:37,764 --> 00:10:43,227
Max speed Mach 3 plus,
ceiling 85,000 feet.

165
00:10:43,228 --> 00:10:45,772
Fastest, highest flying aircraft
in the world.

166
00:10:47,399 --> 00:10:48,441
She's a beauty.

167
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:50,693
She's a beast.

168
00:10:50,694 --> 00:10:51,903
She can outrun a missile.

169
00:10:52,737 --> 00:10:54,196
You'll be in a full pressure suit.

170
00:10:54,197 --> 00:10:56,156
But that won't stop you
from getting shredded

171
00:10:56,157 --> 00:10:58,577
should you decide to eject above Mach 1.

172
00:10:59,786 --> 00:11:02,747
Correct me if I'm wrong, sir,
but isn't this an Air Force op?

173
00:11:03,873 --> 00:11:06,917
It's a black op.
You're flying for the CIA.

174
00:11:06,918 --> 00:11:09,253
- You're decommissioning me.
- Temporarily.

175
00:11:09,254 --> 00:11:11,380
Your training with the cameras
used on the Blackbird

176
00:11:11,381 --> 00:11:13,299
makes you uniquely qualified.

177
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:15,426
You'll be second seat
to an Air Force flyer.

178
00:11:15,427 --> 00:11:17,137
Wait. I'm RIO? I'm not flying?

179
00:11:17,721 --> 00:11:18,805
Not this time, squid.

180
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,016
Major Sanders. Lieutenant Kelly.

181
00:11:22,017 --> 00:11:24,728
The major here's flown 23 sorties
on the Blackbird.

182
00:11:25,896 --> 00:11:27,606
- Nice to meet you.
- Uh-huh.

183
00:11:28,273 --> 00:11:30,441
You ever come under fire in this?

184
00:11:30,442 --> 00:11:32,402
Wouldn't have been doing my job if I had.

185
00:11:33,194 --> 00:11:37,157
This isn't a Navy tac-air beer run.
Recon requires less brawn, more brains.

186
00:11:38,241 --> 00:11:40,076
I can see that. Yeah.

187
00:11:42,913 --> 00:11:45,164
You just keep your eyes on the radar
and let me do the rest.

188
00:11:45,165 --> 00:11:47,249
Got it. Okay, I'm picking up
a bogey with a--

189
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:49,585
just a big old pile of cheek bones
and eyebrows at my 12.

190
00:11:49,586 --> 00:11:52,004
You can fang each
other all you want on the ground here.

191
00:11:52,005 --> 00:11:55,257
But up there, you are one or you are dead.
Remember that.

192
00:11:55,258 --> 00:11:57,426
Understood, sir.
Sorry I made fun of your face.

193
00:11:57,427 --> 00:11:59,763
You just don't see 'em like that
outside of nightmares.

194
00:12:03,391 --> 00:12:05,017
Jesus, Dad.

195
00:12:05,018 --> 00:12:06,810
Hell, I'm fine. I'm fine.

196
00:12:06,811 --> 00:12:09,230
I thought you didn't come home
'cause you got lucky.

197
00:12:09,231 --> 00:12:11,358
Well, I might've. We'll see.

198
00:12:12,275 --> 00:12:13,609
Should I be worried?

199
00:12:13,610 --> 00:12:15,987
No, no, no, no. It's a--
It's a walk in the park.

200
00:12:16,738 --> 00:12:18,739
Which park? Libya?

201
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:19,866
Iran?

202
00:12:20,408 --> 00:12:22,327
That… Well, a classified park actually.

203
00:12:23,995 --> 00:12:26,248
- Well, don't get yourself in any tr--
- No, no. Never do.

204
00:12:27,082 --> 00:12:28,416
Never do. I gotta go.

205
00:12:29,793 --> 00:12:31,503
I… I love you, Pop.

206
00:12:33,797 --> 00:12:34,798
Love you too, pal.

207
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:18,591
Okay.

208
00:13:18,592 --> 00:13:20,134
You're gonna wanna put those in your boot.

209
00:13:20,135 --> 00:13:21,218
Sorry?

210
00:13:21,219 --> 00:13:22,971
The chain can choke you
if you have to eject.

211
00:13:23,889 --> 00:13:25,015
Any zoomie would know that.

212
00:13:25,724 --> 00:13:28,018
Oh, yeah? Zoomies know that?

213
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:38,403
Tank pressure check.

214
00:13:39,154 --> 00:13:42,949
She's at 1.3 PSI. Setting IGV to lockout.

215
00:13:46,328 --> 00:13:49,079
Habu 43, checklist complete?

216
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,373
Affirmative. IGV normal.

217
00:13:51,374 --> 00:13:53,334
OBC camera OP checks good.

218
00:13:53,335 --> 00:13:58,798
Habu 43, wind 265 at five.
Cleared for takeoff, runway 26.

219
00:14:19,819 --> 00:14:22,697
So, Sanders, are you married? Kids?

220
00:14:23,281 --> 00:14:25,200
Not a priority till I make colonel.

221
00:14:25,909 --> 00:14:29,329
Same. You think that's why they chose us?

222
00:14:29,913 --> 00:14:31,081
No ties?

223
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:33,541
You know, we don't have to talk.

224
00:14:36,836 --> 00:14:39,714
You do realize if your dream comes true,
what that'll make you?

225
00:14:41,341 --> 00:14:42,342
What's that?

226
00:14:42,926 --> 00:14:44,344
Colonel Sanders.

227
00:14:47,764 --> 00:14:49,307
No one's ever pointed that out?

228
00:14:52,018 --> 00:14:53,520
1,700 knots.

229
00:14:54,396 --> 00:14:55,897
And 11 herbs and spices.

230
00:15:16,918 --> 00:15:20,338
It's all just one big chunk of land
from up here.

231
00:15:23,675 --> 00:15:25,218
Flight level eight-zero-zero.

232
00:15:26,052 --> 00:15:27,344
Copy that.

233
00:15:27,345 --> 00:15:30,306
Be advised, you are now
crossing Soviet airspace,

234
00:15:30,307 --> 00:15:32,142
512 miles from target.

235
00:15:34,603 --> 00:15:37,564
OBC camera on. Ready.

236
00:15:41,943 --> 00:15:42,944
How are we looking?

237
00:15:43,737 --> 00:15:47,657
Heavy soup over the target.
Doubt we'll get anything clean.

238
00:15:49,034 --> 00:15:51,828
Base, Habu. We've got poor vis.
Please advise.

239
00:15:53,788 --> 00:15:56,291
Habu,
descend to flight level four-five-zero.

240
00:15:57,709 --> 00:15:59,002
First time for everything.

241
00:16:00,462 --> 00:16:02,005
Copy. Four-five-zero.

242
00:16:12,432 --> 00:16:13,600
There we go.

243
00:16:14,434 --> 00:16:17,187
Film is moving. We got eyes on target.

244
00:16:21,107 --> 00:16:24,110
Bravo, zulu. Get back on altitude and RTB.

245
00:16:41,711 --> 00:16:43,505
Bogey one-nine-zero-ten.

246
00:16:45,006 --> 00:16:46,049
Damn it.

247
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:54,808
Tally one Mig, five o'clock.
Jamming engaged and working.

248
00:17:01,940 --> 00:17:04,109
Why are you banking? We'll lose airspeed.

249
00:17:04,651 --> 00:17:05,985
I've got this.

250
00:17:05,986 --> 00:17:07,487
No, you don't. He'll gain on us.

251
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:14,452
See, Kelly? This is why you're
a trunk monkey and I'm a--

252
00:17:17,289 --> 00:17:21,167
Sanders? Sanders, do you copy?

253
00:17:26,506 --> 00:17:29,049
Habu 43, defensive. Scram east.

254
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:31,468
100 miles west of Pechora.

255
00:17:31,469 --> 00:17:33,930
Pilot is unresponsive
and I've lost all flight control.

256
00:17:39,352 --> 00:17:40,270
Come on.

257
00:18:01,583 --> 00:18:02,792
Right engine is bent.

258
00:18:07,464 --> 00:18:08,672
Mayday, mayday, mayday.

259
00:18:08,673 --> 00:18:13,802
Habu 43 marking latitude 65.18,
longitude 72.10.

260
00:18:13,803 --> 00:18:15,012
I'm gonna have to punch out.

261
00:18:15,013 --> 00:18:17,389
You cannot eject at that speed, Assassin!

262
00:18:17,390 --> 00:18:18,683
I know, I know.

263
00:18:24,689 --> 00:18:26,441
That's it. Get up here.

264
00:19:51,568 --> 00:19:52,569
Okay.

265
00:20:33,526 --> 00:20:36,446
What is this? Hey!

266
00:20:40,533 --> 00:20:41,618
Good. You have not died.

267
00:20:43,036 --> 00:20:44,454
Who are you? Where am I?

268
00:20:45,997 --> 00:20:48,165
Well, my name is Nikolai Ustinov.

269
00:20:48,166 --> 00:20:49,416
But you should call me Nick.

270
00:20:49,417 --> 00:20:51,503
And you are in my home.

271
00:20:52,295 --> 00:20:54,380
Welcome. It is an honor.

272
00:20:54,381 --> 00:20:55,715
Why am I tied to the bed?

273
00:20:57,008 --> 00:21:00,220
I tied you so that you would not move
during the surgery.

274
00:21:01,137 --> 00:21:02,263
What do you mean surgery?

275
00:21:02,264 --> 00:21:05,558
The stick in your leg.
I removed it and repaired an artery.

276
00:21:05,559 --> 00:21:07,142
There was a great deal of blood.

277
00:21:07,143 --> 00:21:08,978
You screamed a lot, but that is my fault

278
00:21:08,979 --> 00:21:11,022
because I do not have proper anesthesia.

279
00:21:11,856 --> 00:21:13,275
Can y… can you untie me now?

280
00:21:14,109 --> 00:21:16,861
Of course. Soon, yes.

281
00:21:17,821 --> 00:21:22,617
But I need you to rest now
so that the healing can continue. Uh-huh.

282
00:21:23,243 --> 00:21:27,496
Oh, okay. What is… what is with the…
all the American stuff?

283
00:21:27,497 --> 00:21:33,169
All the… Well, this may shock you,
but I admire your country very much.

284
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:36,755
Your democracy and your culture.

285
00:21:36,756 --> 00:21:37,840
And your food.

286
00:21:37,841 --> 00:21:40,594
I have never had McDonald's,
but I suspect I would love it.

287
00:21:41,177 --> 00:21:42,888
You could almost say I am obsessed.

288
00:21:44,389 --> 00:21:45,681
Oh, is that right?

289
00:21:45,682 --> 00:21:48,727
My dream is to someday live in America.

290
00:21:49,644 --> 00:21:53,315
Drive from sea to shining sea
in a recreational vehicle.

291
00:21:54,316 --> 00:21:56,610
- Fun.
- I don't know yet…

292
00:21:59,070 --> 00:22:00,654
what I would do for work.

293
00:22:00,655 --> 00:22:02,948
But I know that there,
anything is possible.

294
00:22:02,949 --> 00:22:03,950
Yeah.

295
00:22:07,329 --> 00:22:09,247
I have something I want to show you.

296
00:22:22,219 --> 00:22:26,264
This is very special,
but also quite illegal.

297
00:22:28,266 --> 00:22:30,685
A man could go to jail for having this.

298
00:22:31,645 --> 00:22:33,979
I have watched it over 100 times.

299
00:22:33,980 --> 00:22:36,942
And each time,
I imagine I am the man in the movie.

300
00:22:37,943 --> 00:22:40,195
Doing the things that he does.

301
00:22:42,405 --> 00:22:45,407
You see, we don't get
many American films here,

302
00:22:45,408 --> 00:22:48,411
but last year I came upon this bootleg…

303
00:22:49,913 --> 00:22:51,206
of Top Gun.

304
00:22:53,792 --> 00:22:57,337
It confirmed for me
all of my beliefs about your people.

305
00:22:58,129 --> 00:23:00,257
And then, suddenly one day, here you are.

306
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:03,134
Falling from the sky like providence.

307
00:23:03,969 --> 00:23:05,554
- Listen, Nikolai. I'm--
- Stop!

308
00:23:08,473 --> 00:23:10,100
Nick. Call me Nick.

309
00:23:10,725 --> 00:23:13,018
Nick. I'm Troy.

310
00:23:13,019 --> 00:23:16,731
- Troy, nice to meet you.
- I appreciate you patching me up, Nick.

311
00:23:17,983 --> 00:23:19,733
But, as you can imagine,
I really need to get going.

312
00:23:19,734 --> 00:23:21,736
I am behind enemy lines.

313
00:23:22,571 --> 00:23:24,947
Not that… Not that you're an enemy. Right?

314
00:23:24,948 --> 00:23:27,158
Just the opposite, Troy.
I am your biggest fan.

315
00:23:28,243 --> 00:23:30,035
Good. That's good.

316
00:23:30,036 --> 00:23:32,371
So, you'll understand why
I need to get across the border.

317
00:23:32,372 --> 00:23:34,498
Of course. The nearest border is Finland.

318
00:23:34,499 --> 00:23:35,874
How far is that?

319
00:23:35,875 --> 00:23:37,084
2,000 kilometers.

320
00:23:37,085 --> 00:23:38,795
Well, shit.

321
00:23:48,430 --> 00:23:49,848
It's been two years.

322
00:23:50,682 --> 00:23:55,520
Why didn't you do this
when Chernenko died?

323
00:23:58,523 --> 00:24:00,983
It gives me no pleasure
to hang the portrait

324
00:24:00,984 --> 00:24:03,028
of a man who is destroying my country.

325
00:24:03,737 --> 00:24:06,740
Gorbachev would argue he is saving it.

326
00:24:09,534 --> 00:24:12,703
I still remember
when Russia was an empire.

327
00:24:12,704 --> 00:24:15,498
Half the world fell within our influence.
Look at us now.

328
00:24:16,207 --> 00:24:19,710
Losing a bloodless war
to a soulless superpower.

329
00:24:19,711 --> 00:24:24,716
And this bald fool wants us to be
closer to our enemy.

330
00:24:26,551 --> 00:24:27,593
What is it?

331
00:24:27,594 --> 00:24:30,221
An American spy plane shot down
over Khorovaya.

332
00:24:30,222 --> 00:24:32,474
They believe one of the pilots ejected.

333
00:24:33,808 --> 00:24:35,101
Have they secured the crash site?

334
00:24:36,811 --> 00:24:39,272
Not yet.
General Korzhev is leading the search.

335
00:24:42,943 --> 00:24:43,944
Not anymore.

336
00:24:53,787 --> 00:24:56,289
Goose! Goose, hold on!

337
00:25:01,545 --> 00:25:02,461
Oh, God.

338
00:25:02,462 --> 00:25:05,172
Goose and Maverick
were more than copilots.

339
00:25:05,173 --> 00:25:06,674
They were best friends.

340
00:25:06,675 --> 00:25:07,968
Yes, they were.

341
00:25:10,470 --> 00:25:13,180
This is where the man
filming the movie goes to the toilet.

342
00:25:13,181 --> 00:25:14,558
Do you recall what happens here?

343
00:25:15,183 --> 00:25:17,394
I do not. I'm so sorry.

344
00:25:19,521 --> 00:25:21,355
No problem. How is your meat?

345
00:25:21,356 --> 00:25:24,400
Oh, well, this is very, very hard.

346
00:25:24,401 --> 00:25:25,735
But at least it's sour. So…

347
00:25:26,861 --> 00:25:30,447
Yeah, in the winter,
it is difficult to find fresh bear.

348
00:25:30,448 --> 00:25:31,490
I'm eating bear?

349
00:25:31,491 --> 00:25:33,576
Yeah, I have 40 kilos of it
in my root cellar.

350
00:25:33,577 --> 00:25:34,786
Eat as much as you like.

351
00:25:35,287 --> 00:25:36,954
Thank you. What is this?

352
00:25:36,955 --> 00:25:39,290
Samogon. I make it from beets.

353
00:25:39,291 --> 00:25:40,417
In a barrel.

354
00:25:41,251 --> 00:25:42,501
That doesn't taste like beets.

355
00:25:42,502 --> 00:25:44,170
Oh, thank you very much.

356
00:25:45,922 --> 00:25:51,845
I noticed on your flight suit
your call sign is Assassin.

357
00:25:53,346 --> 00:25:55,140
May I ask the origin of this name?

358
00:25:56,057 --> 00:25:58,059
That's a story that only me
and my friends know.

359
00:25:59,769 --> 00:26:00,937
Oh, I see.

360
00:26:03,523 --> 00:26:09,029
I hope someday you and I
will be such friends.

361
00:26:10,530 --> 00:26:14,325
Definitely. I should probably be going.

362
00:26:14,326 --> 00:26:16,952
If you can just untie me,
I'll be on my way.

363
00:26:16,953 --> 00:26:18,871
But if I untie you, you will leave.

364
00:26:18,872 --> 00:26:21,082
Yes. That's what I just said.

365
00:26:21,583 --> 00:26:23,877
I don't think you understand
your situation.

366
00:26:24,628 --> 00:26:27,421
Thousands of kilometers
stand between you and safety.

367
00:26:27,422 --> 00:26:29,883
The Red Army will already
be looking for you.

368
00:26:30,383 --> 00:26:33,511
And when they find you,
they will give you to the KGB.

369
00:26:34,346 --> 00:26:37,223
And that is a fate I would wish on no one.

370
00:26:37,224 --> 00:26:40,268
Believe me, I am your safe haven.

371
00:26:40,769 --> 00:26:42,561
I can't stay here.

372
00:26:42,562 --> 00:26:44,355
Just until the Cold War dies down.

373
00:26:44,356 --> 00:26:46,774
The Cold War has been
going on for 40 years.

374
00:26:46,775 --> 00:26:48,610
Exactly. How much longer can it last?

375
00:26:50,737 --> 00:26:55,324
Okay. Okay. You know what,
you're probably right.

376
00:26:55,325 --> 00:26:58,369
Look, I'm… It would be insane to
try to do this in my condition.

377
00:26:58,370 --> 00:26:59,954
And I would be insane to let you go.

378
00:26:59,955 --> 00:27:01,247
Right. Look, okay.

379
00:27:01,248 --> 00:27:03,792
So, here's what I'll…
I'll stay until it's safe to go.

380
00:27:04,376 --> 00:27:05,585
- Excellent.
- Good.

381
00:27:06,253 --> 00:27:08,629
Are you gonna…
Are you gonna keep me tied up until then?

382
00:27:08,630 --> 00:27:12,883
Of course not. I just needed to know
that we can trust each other, yeah?

383
00:27:12,884 --> 00:27:16,555
I trust you completely. Nick, thank you.

384
00:27:17,055 --> 00:27:18,430
- Yeah, no problem.
- Yeah.

385
00:27:18,431 --> 00:27:19,975
We're going to have a wonderful time.

386
00:27:20,517 --> 00:27:21,351
That's good.

387
00:27:23,979 --> 00:27:25,021
That's better. Okay.

388
00:27:28,692 --> 00:27:29,859
I'm sorry, Nick.

389
00:27:31,987 --> 00:27:33,071
Please stay.

390
00:27:49,129 --> 00:27:50,755
How are you so spry?

391
00:27:53,592 --> 00:27:55,719
Very effective guillotine.

392
00:28:01,766 --> 00:28:04,101
You are damaging yourself.
Let us stop now.

393
00:28:04,102 --> 00:28:05,353
Okay. You win.

394
00:28:08,899 --> 00:28:09,941
Wonderful.

395
00:28:24,456 --> 00:28:25,832
Find the keys. Keys.

396
00:28:36,301 --> 00:28:38,636
Hey! Come back inside, my friend.

397
00:28:38,637 --> 00:28:39,638
I will make tea.

398
00:30:53,980 --> 00:30:56,815
Please connect me to
the US Embassy in Moscow. Quickly.

399
00:30:56,816 --> 00:30:57,651
Qui--

400
00:31:01,696 --> 00:31:05,283
This is for you. Practicing English.

401
00:31:06,159 --> 00:31:08,078
Okay. No, no, no. Hey, hey, hey.

402
00:31:09,496 --> 00:31:10,580
I'm leaving. Okay? I--

403
00:31:11,248 --> 00:31:13,208
Okay. Listen to me. It's fine. It's--

404
00:31:21,925 --> 00:31:23,009
Don't--

405
00:32:52,557 --> 00:32:53,641
All right.

406
00:32:53,642 --> 00:32:54,476
Nikolai!

407
00:32:55,227 --> 00:32:56,937
What have you done?

408
00:32:59,356 --> 00:33:00,690
This should settle their tab.

409
00:33:06,780 --> 00:33:10,783
Who are you?
Where did you learn to fight like that?

410
00:33:10,784 --> 00:33:13,911
I'm sure you would have held your own
if not for your injury.

411
00:33:13,912 --> 00:33:16,665
American combat training
is far superior to ours.

412
00:33:17,374 --> 00:33:19,542
"Ours"? You were military?

413
00:33:20,168 --> 00:33:21,336
It doesn't matter.

414
00:33:22,379 --> 00:33:25,006
Well, it matters to me.
I wanna know who I'm sitting here with.

415
00:33:29,844 --> 00:33:31,805
Years ago, I was a state security officer.

416
00:33:32,639 --> 00:33:36,101
Hold on. You're KGB?
What do you do for them?

417
00:33:36,893 --> 00:33:38,186
Nothing now.

418
00:33:38,770 --> 00:33:42,148
I led a…
a team that carried out covert ops.

419
00:33:42,691 --> 00:33:45,776
Counterintelligence. Interrogation.

420
00:33:45,777 --> 00:33:47,152
Oh, so you're a monster.

421
00:33:47,153 --> 00:33:49,614
I believed I was acting
in the interest of my country.

422
00:33:51,116 --> 00:33:52,032
Right.

423
00:33:52,033 --> 00:33:55,494
But when my daughter grew old enough
to ask me what I did when I went to work,

424
00:33:55,495 --> 00:33:58,707
I was too ashamed to tell her.

425
00:33:59,791 --> 00:34:02,084
You see, when a man does something
for long enough,

426
00:34:02,085 --> 00:34:03,420
it stops being what he does.

427
00:34:04,921 --> 00:34:06,339
It becomes who he is.

428
00:34:09,925 --> 00:34:13,429
So I'm supposed to buy that you
just washed your hands of all this,

429
00:34:13,430 --> 00:34:15,891
moved up here
and became Grizzly Adams? Is that right?

430
00:34:16,599 --> 00:34:20,603
I had to put myself
as far from the regime as I could.

431
00:34:20,604 --> 00:34:23,397
And I need to put myself
as far from you as I can.

432
00:34:23,398 --> 00:34:26,651
Listen to me. If I were still
that monster, why would I take you in?

433
00:34:27,527 --> 00:34:29,820
Why would I nurse you
and fight those men at the bar?

434
00:34:30,488 --> 00:34:32,865
I've aided an enemy of the Republic.

435
00:34:33,992 --> 00:34:35,660
That is punishable by death.

436
00:34:40,289 --> 00:34:42,208
I appreciate you helping me out.

437
00:34:43,835 --> 00:34:46,545
- I'm sorry I set you on fire.
- You were trying to get home.

438
00:34:46,546 --> 00:34:47,712
Lot of good it did me.

439
00:34:47,713 --> 00:34:49,883
I couldn't even get a call
through to the embassy.

440
00:34:51,468 --> 00:34:55,137
Even if you had, you'd only be
bringing state security to our door.

441
00:34:55,972 --> 00:34:58,225
The government monitors all calls
to foreign embassies.

442
00:35:00,101 --> 00:35:02,144
- What if I called on this?
- That's a relic.

443
00:35:02,145 --> 00:35:04,606
It's a 30 kilometer range on a good day.

444
00:35:05,232 --> 00:35:08,276
The only way is
if you had access to an Altai.

445
00:35:09,569 --> 00:35:12,363
- A what?
- It's a mobile radiotelephone.

446
00:35:12,364 --> 00:35:14,156
They can't be traced.
They're not monitored.

447
00:35:14,157 --> 00:35:15,908
Okay. How do I get one of those?

448
00:35:15,909 --> 00:35:18,911
You don't. They're only available
to high-placed government officials.

449
00:35:18,912 --> 00:35:21,121
And I'm guessing you don't have
a lot of those out here?

450
00:35:21,122 --> 00:35:22,039
No. Not here.

451
00:35:22,040 --> 00:35:24,875
- Out in Lake… Lake Vozhe, though.
- Lake Vozhe?

452
00:35:24,876 --> 00:35:28,379
Many of the members of
the Supreme Soviet have dachas there.

453
00:35:28,380 --> 00:35:29,880
Is that close?

454
00:35:29,881 --> 00:35:33,635
It's about
halfway between here and Moscow.

455
00:35:34,511 --> 00:35:37,137
Perfect! We're gonna steal an Altai,

456
00:35:37,138 --> 00:35:39,849
I'm gonna call the embassy and
they're gonna get me the hell out of here.

457
00:35:41,434 --> 00:35:42,560
What?

458
00:35:42,561 --> 00:35:44,771
You would be rescued, but I…

459
00:35:46,064 --> 00:35:47,065
Right.

460
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:49,943
What if I take you with me to the States?

461
00:35:50,777 --> 00:35:52,611
Soviets cannot emigrate, Troy.

462
00:35:52,612 --> 00:35:54,989
No, not normally.
But I'm a shot-down pilot.

463
00:35:54,990 --> 00:35:57,741
I'm gonna be a national hero. They'll
probably give me the Medal of Honor.

464
00:35:57,742 --> 00:35:59,618
There's no way the embassy's gonna
say no to me, Nick.

465
00:35:59,619 --> 00:36:00,995
Unfortunately, it's not so simple.

466
00:36:00,996 --> 00:36:03,372
I have a daughter in Moscow.
I cannot leave without her.

467
00:36:03,373 --> 00:36:04,331
We'll take her along.

468
00:36:04,332 --> 00:36:09,670
She wouldn't come. She does not
believe that I am a changed man.

469
00:36:09,671 --> 00:36:11,381
Talk to her. Make her believe it.

470
00:36:11,965 --> 00:36:18,638
Russians are not as comfortable
sharing their feelings as your people.

471
00:36:19,222 --> 00:36:22,391
You said that your dream
was to become an American.

472
00:36:22,392 --> 00:36:24,853
Start acting like an American.

473
00:36:26,021 --> 00:36:27,314
Nick, will you help me?

474
00:36:30,609 --> 00:36:35,362
This is very tempting,
but it is also very dangerous.

475
00:36:35,363 --> 00:36:38,491
Hey. Isn't it about high time that we

476
00:36:39,826 --> 00:36:41,578
"ride into the danger zone"?

477
00:36:43,914 --> 00:36:44,998
Kenny Loggins.

478
00:36:46,583 --> 00:36:47,708
I understand this joke.

479
00:36:47,709 --> 00:36:48,919
We got a deal?

480
00:36:51,171 --> 00:36:53,839
Let me finish my drink first
before I decide.

481
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,674
Of course.

482
00:36:55,634 --> 00:36:56,718
I'll drink to that.

483
00:37:25,747 --> 00:37:26,790
Down the hatch.

484
00:37:35,090 --> 00:37:36,340
Come on, man,

485
00:37:36,341 --> 00:37:37,926
it's the world's smallest glass!

486
00:38:05,161 --> 00:38:07,162
May I help you, Comrade?

487
00:38:07,163 --> 00:38:09,624
Alexander Volkov. State Security.
May I come in?

488
00:38:17,674 --> 00:38:19,634
You live alone here, I take it?

489
00:38:20,886 --> 00:38:21,886
Yes.

490
00:38:21,887 --> 00:38:23,138
What is this about?

491
00:38:23,930 --> 00:38:26,056
An aircraft went down
12 kilometers from here.

492
00:38:26,057 --> 00:38:30,020
We are asking local residents whether
they heard or saw anything of interest.

493
00:38:32,105 --> 00:38:33,648
No, sir.

494
00:38:34,691 --> 00:38:35,692
I see.

495
00:38:42,324 --> 00:38:44,075
My daughter, Anna.

496
00:38:45,410 --> 00:38:46,912
You were KGB?

497
00:38:48,038 --> 00:38:48,996
How…

498
00:38:48,997 --> 00:38:50,749
Your signet ring.

499
00:38:51,791 --> 00:38:53,501
Division?

500
00:38:54,502 --> 00:38:55,795
Alpha Group.

501
00:39:01,092 --> 00:39:02,384
I commend you for your service.

502
00:39:02,385 --> 00:39:03,929
What made you leave?

503
00:39:05,096 --> 00:39:07,057
My mind was becoming less sharp.

504
00:39:09,976 --> 00:39:12,187
You strike me as having a very sharp mind.

505
00:39:25,784 --> 00:39:27,369
What is down here?

506
00:39:28,245 --> 00:39:29,412
Root cellar.

507
00:39:30,038 --> 00:39:31,539
Humor me.

508
00:39:32,958 --> 00:39:35,418
There is nothing.

509
00:39:41,341 --> 00:39:42,676
Very well.

510
00:39:54,145 --> 00:39:55,605
I've caught you!

511
00:40:00,193 --> 00:40:01,235
Samogon?

512
00:40:01,236 --> 00:40:02,403
Yes…

513
00:40:02,404 --> 00:40:05,740
You do know that home distilling
of spirits is against the law?

514
00:40:06,241 --> 00:40:08,617
I'm sorry, Comrade Volkov. I didn't know--

515
00:40:08,618 --> 00:40:09,661
Please.

516
00:40:10,453 --> 00:40:12,037
I will make you a deal.

517
00:40:12,038 --> 00:40:13,747
You share a glass with me

518
00:40:13,748 --> 00:40:15,375
and it will be our secret.

519
00:40:17,043 --> 00:40:19,087
Of course.

520
00:40:40,191 --> 00:40:41,400
You can taste the beets.

521
00:40:41,401 --> 00:40:42,986
Thank you very much.

522
00:40:44,613 --> 00:40:48,617
Reminds me of the moonshine
we had in Prague in '68.

523
00:40:49,117 --> 00:40:51,244
I was a lowly junior lieutenant.

524
00:40:51,912 --> 00:40:55,915
We spent two months in the barracks
with very little to do.

525
00:40:55,916 --> 00:40:57,125
So we drank.

526
00:40:59,044 --> 00:41:01,338
You must miss it.

527
00:41:02,380 --> 00:41:03,632
The camaraderie.

528
00:41:04,216 --> 00:41:07,427
The sacrifices we make for our motherland.

529
00:41:09,471 --> 00:41:12,015
I think about it every day.

530
00:41:15,435 --> 00:41:16,519
Well,

531
00:41:17,270 --> 00:41:18,855
thank you for your hospitality.

532
00:41:20,565 --> 00:41:22,191
I must continue my survey.

533
00:41:22,192 --> 00:41:23,693
Certainly.

534
00:41:24,277 --> 00:41:28,907
I trust I can find you here
should we need to speak again?

535
00:41:30,575 --> 00:41:32,493
If anything occurs to you,

536
00:41:32,494 --> 00:41:34,037
do not hesitate to call.

537
00:41:35,538 --> 00:41:37,457
I wish you continued good health.

538
00:41:38,208 --> 00:41:39,501
You and your daughter.

539
00:41:49,386 --> 00:41:50,387
Christ.

540
00:41:52,013 --> 00:41:53,847
Thought you were gonna ask him
to stay for dinner.

541
00:41:53,848 --> 00:41:55,766
- This is bad.
- What do you mean? He left.

542
00:41:55,767 --> 00:41:58,102
He will speak to the men at the bar.
They will identify us.

543
00:41:58,103 --> 00:41:59,687
We must leave immediately.

544
00:41:59,688 --> 00:42:02,273
Well, I'll tell ya something.
That Samogon stings.

545
00:42:02,274 --> 00:42:03,608
Front and back, Nick.

546
00:42:12,826 --> 00:42:14,536
I don't know if it's safe
to drive that way.

547
00:42:15,078 --> 00:42:16,870
There's no time for safety.

548
00:42:16,871 --> 00:42:19,291
I'm getting a lot of your beard
in my mouth.

549
00:42:20,584 --> 00:42:23,752
Okay. Can we just, maybe…
maybe just put your hands on the wheel

550
00:42:23,753 --> 00:42:24,837
or slow down a little?

551
00:42:24,838 --> 00:42:27,089
We don't know whether they have
connected us yet.

552
00:42:27,090 --> 00:42:28,549
We need to change our appearance.

553
00:42:28,550 --> 00:42:31,011
Well, if we hit a tree,
that'll change our appearance.

554
00:42:40,061 --> 00:42:42,146
How long is the drive to Lake Vozhe?

555
00:42:42,147 --> 00:42:43,314
Three days.

556
00:42:43,315 --> 00:42:45,442
But we will get there in one.

557
00:42:46,234 --> 00:42:47,235
How's that?

558
00:42:49,779 --> 00:42:51,656
- We're not driving.
- What're you doing?

559
00:42:52,198 --> 00:42:53,491
They'll be looking for my truck.

560
00:42:54,075 --> 00:42:55,076
So?

561
00:42:55,869 --> 00:42:57,077
You'll want to get out.

562
00:42:57,078 --> 00:42:58,914
What? Why?

563
00:43:01,374 --> 00:43:02,375
Yep.

564
00:43:06,421 --> 00:43:07,631
Is this a lake?

565
00:43:08,465 --> 00:43:10,549
You could've told me
you were gonna do that.

566
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:13,594
I apologize. I assumed you knew
standard tracking evasion.

567
00:43:13,595 --> 00:43:15,804
Do they not train pilots in such methods?

568
00:43:15,805 --> 00:43:19,267
No, Nick. No, they don't train us
to hide our planes in frozen lakes.

569
00:43:20,435 --> 00:43:21,394
Where are we going?

570
00:43:22,020 --> 00:43:24,314
Railroad station. Through here.

571
00:43:25,941 --> 00:43:28,443
Somehow, your beard is
still attacking my mouth.

572
00:43:34,157 --> 00:43:39,913
Our divisions are searching
the north and eastern edges of the forest.

573
00:43:40,956 --> 00:43:44,209
The second pilot landed here.

574
00:43:46,836 --> 00:43:48,254
No body?

575
00:43:48,255 --> 00:43:49,672
He survived.

576
00:43:49,673 --> 00:43:51,550
The snow has covered his tracks.

577
00:44:02,310 --> 00:44:03,394
His boot.

578
00:44:03,395 --> 00:44:05,854
We are waiting for
equipment to retrieve it.

579
00:44:05,855 --> 00:44:07,023
Hold this.

580
00:44:43,226 --> 00:44:44,853
Find his photograph.

581
00:44:46,229 --> 00:44:47,939
Get it in front of all security personnel.

582
00:45:06,166 --> 00:45:08,752
Couldn't have shot us down
closer to the border?

583
00:45:10,295 --> 00:45:11,379
"Us"?

584
00:45:12,088 --> 00:45:13,881
Yeah, I had a copilot, Sanders. He…

585
00:45:13,882 --> 00:45:15,133
He didn't make it.

586
00:45:15,634 --> 00:45:16,635
I'm sorry.

587
00:45:17,636 --> 00:45:20,387
He was an asshole, but he deserved better.

588
00:45:20,388 --> 00:45:23,767
It takes great courage
to be a fighter pilot.

589
00:45:26,019 --> 00:45:27,270
I suppose so, yeah.

590
00:45:28,396 --> 00:45:29,898
It's all I ever wanted to do.

591
00:45:31,441 --> 00:45:35,862
Actually, I wanted to build ships
for the Navy like my dad.

592
00:45:37,447 --> 00:45:42,034
Then when I was eight,
he took me onboard the USS Randolph

593
00:45:42,035 --> 00:45:44,537
to watch the F-9s land for CQ…

594
00:45:46,831 --> 00:45:49,667
and the way those guys
walked across the flight deck

595
00:45:49,668 --> 00:45:53,672
with their helmets in their hands,
and everybody, including my dad,

596
00:45:55,340 --> 00:45:57,342
looked at them like they were gods,
and then…

597
00:45:57,842 --> 00:46:00,512
then that was it. I was… I was hooked.

598
00:46:02,639 --> 00:46:04,349
So you wanted to be God.

599
00:46:07,602 --> 00:46:10,479
I wanted to serve my country.
I think you can understand that.

600
00:46:10,480 --> 00:46:12,523
Fear drove me to serve mine.

601
00:46:12,524 --> 00:46:14,901
We were told that
America would destroy us.

602
00:46:15,485 --> 00:46:18,779
That your greed and soullessness
would bring the end of humanity.

603
00:46:18,780 --> 00:46:21,532
And we were taught that you were cogs
in a giant world-killing machine.

604
00:46:21,533 --> 00:46:23,492
We were both fed lies.

605
00:46:23,493 --> 00:46:24,743
I wasn't fed lies.

606
00:46:24,744 --> 00:46:27,246
It was Khrushchev that said,
"We will bury you."

607
00:46:27,247 --> 00:46:30,499
And Reagan called us the evil empire.
Do you believe we are all evil?

608
00:46:30,500 --> 00:46:31,750
I believe you're brainwashed.

609
00:46:31,751 --> 00:46:33,544
Products of the system
that you grew up in.

610
00:46:33,545 --> 00:46:36,756
But you are not
a product of your system, Troy?

611
00:46:41,636 --> 00:46:43,263
Don't you KGB me.

612
00:46:46,516 --> 00:46:48,226
I'm going to rest my eyes.

613
00:46:49,394 --> 00:46:52,272
Please wake me when
we get to Starokostyantynivske.

614
00:46:53,189 --> 00:46:55,525
I don't see any reason why
I won't be able to do that.

615
00:47:40,862 --> 00:47:43,448
Nick. Wake up.

616
00:47:48,995 --> 00:47:50,997
I think we need to change cars.

617
00:47:59,548 --> 00:48:00,715
Now I've got herpes.

618
00:48:18,692 --> 00:48:20,652
Nick, I really need you to wake up.

619
00:48:26,116 --> 00:48:27,450
Don't look in the folder.

620
00:48:31,121 --> 00:48:32,998
Yeah, he's showing his friends.

621
00:48:57,022 --> 00:48:58,105
Nice nap?

622
00:48:58,106 --> 00:49:00,483
Comrades, I am an officer of the KGB.

623
00:49:01,067 --> 00:49:04,362
I am delivering this prisoner
to my superiors.

624
00:49:05,906 --> 00:49:06,989
Why should we believe you?

625
00:49:06,990 --> 00:49:08,991
Why would I lie to my brothers-in-arms?

626
00:49:08,992 --> 00:49:10,993
Listen to me right now!

627
00:49:10,994 --> 00:49:12,494
I'm doing this to convey the impression

628
00:49:12,495 --> 00:49:13,954
- that you are my prisoner.
- Okay.

629
00:49:13,955 --> 00:49:16,917
But this ruse will not last for long.

630
00:49:20,670 --> 00:49:22,589
In 30 seconds,
this train will enter a tunnel.

631
00:49:23,215 --> 00:49:25,300
There will be a moment before
the carriage lights come on.

632
00:49:26,051 --> 00:49:27,134
Hey!

633
00:49:27,135 --> 00:49:28,594
I am so sorry.

634
00:49:28,595 --> 00:49:29,929
What the hell?

635
00:49:29,930 --> 00:49:32,349
In that moment,
we run toward the front of the train.

636
00:49:33,141 --> 00:49:34,225
Comrade.

637
00:49:34,226 --> 00:49:37,686
These credentials expired ten years ago.

638
00:49:37,687 --> 00:49:38,646
Did they?

639
00:49:38,647 --> 00:49:40,190
I am taking you both into custody.

640
00:49:41,816 --> 00:49:43,026
Why?

641
00:49:46,738 --> 00:49:47,655
There!

642
00:49:47,656 --> 00:49:49,115
Stop them!

643
00:49:55,288 --> 00:49:57,791
What'd you put us on?
A goddamn troop train?

644
00:50:29,698 --> 00:50:31,073
We must jump.

645
00:50:31,074 --> 00:50:34,744
All right. On three. Two. One.

646
00:50:36,580 --> 00:50:37,581
Jesus.

647
00:50:40,709 --> 00:50:43,753
- We're running out of train.
- As long as we run out of tunnel first.

648
00:51:04,524 --> 00:51:05,859
We're almost out.

649
00:51:21,917 --> 00:51:24,377
Maybe we should've waited
till the Cold War is over.

650
00:51:33,511 --> 00:51:35,639
We need to find shelter for the night.

651
00:51:36,139 --> 00:51:37,890
Think there's a Red Roof Inn here?

652
00:51:37,891 --> 00:51:39,392
I don't know what that is.

653
00:51:40,393 --> 00:51:42,019
Where are you going?

654
00:51:42,020 --> 00:51:43,188
I'm finding shelter.

655
00:51:46,483 --> 00:51:47,733
Do you know these people?

656
00:51:47,734 --> 00:51:48,735
No. Why would I?

657
00:52:03,250 --> 00:52:05,876
- What did you say to her?
- That we are cold and hungry.

658
00:52:05,877 --> 00:52:07,503
And she's just gonna let us in?

659
00:52:07,504 --> 00:52:09,589
And you said we were all evil.

660
00:52:19,975 --> 00:52:20,891
Vodka.

661
00:52:20,892 --> 00:52:22,434
- That--
- She says, "Please enjoy."

662
00:52:22,435 --> 00:52:24,270
Okay, thank-- No, thank you.

663
00:52:24,271 --> 00:52:25,354
Okay.

664
00:52:25,355 --> 00:52:28,566
Are you sure that this is a good idea,
bringing an American in here?

665
00:52:28,567 --> 00:52:30,067
I told them you were my cousin.

666
00:52:30,068 --> 00:52:34,405
What if they've seen my picture on TV?
They could call the authorities.

667
00:52:34,406 --> 00:52:35,740
You see a television here?

668
00:52:36,616 --> 00:52:39,035
- It could be in the other room.
- Do you see another room?

669
00:52:41,663 --> 00:52:43,247
- No, I do not see…
- Please.

670
00:52:43,248 --> 00:52:45,083
…another room. Okay. Thank you. All right.

671
00:52:45,667 --> 00:52:47,210
This looks delicious.

672
00:52:55,343 --> 00:52:57,178
What is with the kid?

673
00:52:58,096 --> 00:52:59,722
I'm guessing these
aren't his parents, right?

674
00:52:59,723 --> 00:53:01,641
Although, that would explain a lot.

675
00:53:09,024 --> 00:53:10,107
His name is Gorgo.

676
00:53:10,108 --> 00:53:12,568
His parents had to move
to Moscow to find work.

677
00:53:12,569 --> 00:53:14,945
So, now he stays here
with his grandparents.

678
00:53:14,946 --> 00:53:18,074
Oh, hey. Hey, Gorgo. What's up?

679
00:53:20,368 --> 00:53:23,288
Okay. Just gonna pull that away.

680
00:53:31,922 --> 00:53:34,590
His parents send money back here,
but every day it is a struggle.

681
00:53:34,591 --> 00:53:38,594
Sometimes they must decide between
coal for the stove or food for the table.

682
00:53:38,595 --> 00:53:40,347
Yeah?

683
00:53:40,889 --> 00:53:42,641
Well, then why… why would they let us in?

684
00:53:44,226 --> 00:53:47,895
If someone came to the door
in America and asked for help,

685
00:53:47,896 --> 00:53:49,439
wouldn't they be taken in?

686
00:53:50,774 --> 00:53:51,942
Of course they would.

687
00:53:56,238 --> 00:53:57,239
Thank you.

688
00:54:05,956 --> 00:54:08,832
It's interesting.
They taught you so many ways to fight us,

689
00:54:08,833 --> 00:54:11,753
but you've never learned
the first thing about us.

690
00:54:13,672 --> 00:54:16,091
Do you know the cormorant bird?

691
00:54:16,883 --> 00:54:19,802
You are… What?
You are all over the map tonight.

692
00:54:19,803 --> 00:54:23,138
When hunting fish, the cormorant will dive
60 feet below the sea

693
00:54:23,139 --> 00:54:25,391
and remain underwater for over a minute.

694
00:54:25,392 --> 00:54:27,726
Out of its element. Completely vulnerable.

695
00:54:27,727 --> 00:54:31,273
But the only way for the bird
to understand the fish

696
00:54:31,982 --> 00:54:33,567
is by swimming with them.

697
00:54:36,861 --> 00:54:38,154
Just gonna…

698
00:54:48,582 --> 00:54:50,333
Are we all sleeping in the same room?

699
00:55:11,021 --> 00:55:13,315
Apparently, Lake Vozhe
is just down this road.

700
00:55:16,234 --> 00:55:17,485
Hey. Hey…

701
00:55:19,487 --> 00:55:21,530
Look, that's… That's…

702
00:55:21,531 --> 00:55:23,742
That's for you. You take that.

703
00:55:25,285 --> 00:55:27,077
No, no, that's the least I can do.

704
00:55:27,078 --> 00:55:28,830
You take it.

705
00:55:33,084 --> 00:55:34,668
Okay. All right, thank you.

706
00:55:34,669 --> 00:55:35,920
Okay.

707
00:55:35,921 --> 00:55:37,504
That felt good. All right.

708
00:55:37,505 --> 00:55:39,507
Let's not make the missus jealous.
All right.

709
00:55:40,675 --> 00:55:41,676
Get out of here.

710
00:55:43,845 --> 00:55:45,472
That was a very nice gesture.

711
00:55:46,097 --> 00:55:48,016
It's worth more than
he would make in a year.

712
00:55:48,934 --> 00:55:52,854
Maybe they can finally afford to get
little Gorgo a proper cage with a lock.

713
00:55:57,651 --> 00:56:00,070
You know, I feel sorry for him
in many ways.

714
00:56:00,987 --> 00:56:02,071
For Gorgo?

715
00:56:02,072 --> 00:56:03,073
Yes, Gorgo.

716
00:56:03,615 --> 00:56:05,659
- He's a demon, Nick.
- He's unusual.

717
00:56:06,368 --> 00:56:07,994
Looked a demon right in the eyes.

718
00:56:17,796 --> 00:56:20,340
Yeah, those are
not private security. They're KGB.

719
00:56:21,466 --> 00:56:23,635
Only an apparatchik would
have such protection.

720
00:56:25,136 --> 00:56:26,512
So whoever lives in this dacha

721
00:56:26,513 --> 00:56:28,806
- has an Altai phone?
- More than likely.

722
00:56:28,807 --> 00:56:31,892
There's no car in the driveway. Meaning
our man is in town, but not at home.

723
00:56:31,893 --> 00:56:32,935
Good timing.

724
00:56:32,936 --> 00:56:34,353
So how are you gonna get past these guys?

725
00:56:34,354 --> 00:56:36,689
They're walking
a standard vos'merka patrol pattern.

726
00:56:36,690 --> 00:56:39,359
We simply wait for
the seredina gap to present itself.

727
00:56:41,528 --> 00:56:43,488
- So I'll follow you?
- You will follow me.

728
00:56:48,034 --> 00:56:49,201
What are you doing?

729
00:56:49,202 --> 00:56:50,537
Looking for their channel.

730
00:56:51,454 --> 00:56:52,831
Yeah, here it is.

731
00:56:58,628 --> 00:56:59,880
Go. Go, go.

732
00:57:03,508 --> 00:57:05,509
You learn that trick in the KGB?

733
00:57:05,510 --> 00:57:08,512
No. Young Pioneers. Like your Boy Scouts.

734
00:57:08,513 --> 00:57:13,058
Well, the Scouts taught me how to build
a very slow car out of a block of wood.

735
00:57:13,059 --> 00:57:14,226
If that comes in handy.

736
00:57:14,227 --> 00:57:15,228
It won't.

737
00:57:18,523 --> 00:57:19,691
Young Pioneers again?

738
00:57:20,567 --> 00:57:21,610
KGB.

739
00:57:28,658 --> 00:57:31,118
Okay, you search upstairs.
Stay in contact.

740
00:57:31,119 --> 00:57:32,120
Roger that.

741
00:57:32,829 --> 00:57:34,914
Wait, hold on.
I don't know what this phone looks like.

742
00:57:34,915 --> 00:57:37,750
Small briefcase.
About the size of a human baby.

743
00:57:37,751 --> 00:57:38,752
Got it.

744
00:57:46,885 --> 00:57:48,762
And this is the one they chose to frame.

745
00:58:06,488 --> 00:58:07,489
Neat.

746
00:58:08,698 --> 00:58:09,866
Nick.

747
00:58:13,119 --> 00:58:14,703
Troy, I have the phone.

748
00:58:14,704 --> 00:58:17,624
Oh, good. We can use it
to call a therapist for this child.

749
00:58:19,668 --> 00:58:21,253
- Here.
- Oh, that's good.

750
00:58:21,753 --> 00:58:23,712
When we get a safe distance
from the house,

751
00:58:23,713 --> 00:58:25,006
then you can make your call.

752
00:58:41,439 --> 00:58:43,358
That is not his wife.

753
00:58:44,192 --> 00:58:45,193
Uh-huh.

754
00:58:46,861 --> 00:58:49,698
She is a sexual escort.

755
00:58:50,490 --> 00:58:52,701
I can see that. Thank you.

756
00:58:55,370 --> 00:58:58,164
I meant to ask
now that we've grown closer,

757
00:58:58,999 --> 00:59:01,501
will you tell me
why they call you Assassin?

758
00:59:02,794 --> 00:59:05,462
Really?
For real, you're asking me this now?

759
00:59:05,463 --> 00:59:06,506
I'm very curious.

760
00:59:07,340 --> 00:59:08,674
It's private.

761
00:59:08,675 --> 00:59:09,843
I thought we were closer.

762
00:59:10,802 --> 00:59:11,803
We're not.

763
00:59:16,766 --> 00:59:18,934
Oh, she is unclothing him.

764
00:59:18,935 --> 00:59:21,729
Okay. I… I don't need the play-by-play.

765
00:59:21,730 --> 00:59:24,064
- But thank you.
- Let us hope this is merely the foreplay

766
00:59:24,065 --> 00:59:26,150
and they move upstairs
for the act of intercourse.

767
00:59:26,151 --> 00:59:29,195
You are scorching my ear
with the heat of your breath.

768
00:59:34,743 --> 00:59:37,202
Shit! It's my family!

769
00:59:37,203 --> 00:59:38,579
You said they were coming tomorrow!

770
00:59:38,580 --> 00:59:39,581
Quickly!

771
00:59:41,958 --> 00:59:43,959
Not that way! She'll see you!

772
00:59:43,960 --> 00:59:45,044
In there!

773
00:59:45,045 --> 00:59:46,838
Oh, she is coming here.

774
00:59:58,600 --> 00:59:59,684
Who are you?

775
01:00:01,102 --> 01:00:02,395
Burglars.

776
01:00:05,899 --> 01:00:07,441
Nadia! What are you doing here?

777
01:00:07,442 --> 01:00:09,361
We came up early to avoid traffic.

778
01:00:09,861 --> 01:00:11,445
Are you not happy to see us?

779
01:00:11,446 --> 01:00:12,655
Of course I'm happy.

780
01:00:12,656 --> 01:00:15,491
I have such a headache. I need some wine.

781
01:00:15,492 --> 01:00:16,992
I will get it.

782
01:00:16,993 --> 01:00:18,036
You sit down.

783
01:00:19,621 --> 01:00:21,331
And now the man is coming.

784
01:00:43,979 --> 01:00:46,063
My head has been pounding
since this morning.

785
01:00:46,064 --> 01:00:48,232
Please. No more whining.
You sound like the children.

786
01:00:48,233 --> 01:00:49,441
I'll draw you a bath.

787
01:00:49,442 --> 01:00:50,526
Don't rush me.

788
01:00:50,527 --> 01:00:52,779
The car ride was so tiring today.

789
01:01:06,293 --> 01:01:08,795
- Yeah?
- There's a call for you, sir.

790
01:01:09,504 --> 01:01:10,505
At this hour?

791
01:01:11,381 --> 01:01:15,260
If he is who he says he is,
you're gonna want to take it.

792
01:01:17,095 --> 01:01:20,222
This is Consul General Hennessy.
To whom am I speaking?

793
01:01:20,223 --> 01:01:24,768
This is Lieutenant Troy Kelly.
US Navy service number E02-77-41.

794
01:01:24,769 --> 01:01:27,187
I'm behind enemy lines
and I need immediate evac.

795
01:01:27,188 --> 01:01:29,648
Hold on, Lieutenant.
This line might not be secure.

796
01:01:29,649 --> 01:01:32,067
I'm calling from
a Russian Altai radiotelephone.

797
01:01:32,068 --> 01:01:33,611
There's no way they can monitor this.

798
01:01:33,612 --> 01:01:36,488
- How the hell did you get that?
- That's not important.

799
01:01:36,489 --> 01:01:38,490
All right, look,
if I give you my approximate location,

800
01:01:38,491 --> 01:01:40,534
how quickly can you dispatch an S&R team?

801
01:01:40,535 --> 01:01:41,493
Okay, hold on.

802
01:01:41,494 --> 01:01:43,204
It's not that simple.

803
01:01:44,080 --> 01:01:45,623
You were in a black op.

804
01:01:45,624 --> 01:01:47,791
The US can't recognize
your presence in this country.

805
01:01:47,792 --> 01:01:51,587
An evac on Russian soil would be
an admission that we engaged in espionage.

806
01:01:51,588 --> 01:01:52,923
So what am I supposed to do?

807
01:01:54,466 --> 01:01:57,885
If you can make it across
the border or to our embassy in Moscow,

808
01:01:57,886 --> 01:01:59,178
we would have plenipotentiary.

809
01:01:59,179 --> 01:02:01,473
We could get you home.
Do you have a vehicle?

810
01:02:04,601 --> 01:02:05,602
Yes, I do.

811
01:02:06,811 --> 01:02:09,773
There's one more thing.
There's a Russian guy.

812
01:02:10,315 --> 01:02:11,398
He's been helping me out.

813
01:02:11,399 --> 01:02:15,694
His name is Nick… Nikolai Ustinov.
I promised him and his daughter asylum.

814
01:02:15,695 --> 01:02:17,404
I'll have to clear that
with the ambassador.

815
01:02:17,405 --> 01:02:19,741
Well, you do that.
We'll call you when we get to Moscow.

816
01:02:21,409 --> 01:02:23,035
Did they give you an extraction point?

817
01:02:23,036 --> 01:02:26,122
Yeah, the embassy in Moscow.
They want us to go to them.

818
01:02:26,748 --> 01:02:31,503
But you are an American hero.
Why would they not come get you?

819
01:02:32,754 --> 01:02:34,798
Well, I guess
there's bigger things at stake.

820
01:02:36,550 --> 01:02:38,718
Okay. We will have to
pick up my daughter first.

821
01:02:39,302 --> 01:02:41,304
I will page her and ask her address.

822
01:02:41,805 --> 01:02:44,558
- You don't know where she lives?
- She moves around a lot.

823
01:02:45,850 --> 01:02:47,268
There is good news though.

824
01:02:47,269 --> 01:02:48,644
What's that?

825
01:02:48,645 --> 01:02:50,105
We have a cassette player.

826
01:02:51,523 --> 01:02:53,525
Twelve hours of that one tape.

827
01:02:56,987 --> 01:02:58,529
Who is the daddy in the song?

828
01:02:58,530 --> 01:03:00,657
You know,
I've always wondered that myself.

829
01:03:51,124 --> 01:03:53,542
It is too late
to get into the embassy tonight.

830
01:03:53,543 --> 01:03:55,170
We will stay with my daughter.

831
01:03:56,463 --> 01:03:58,005
If she allows us.

832
01:03:58,006 --> 01:03:59,924
Moscow always this angry?

833
01:03:59,925 --> 01:04:02,343
They're preparing for
the Mayday parade tomorrow.

834
01:04:02,344 --> 01:04:04,303
A celebration of Soviet might.

835
01:04:04,304 --> 01:04:06,973
The streets will be filled
with soldiers and weapons.

836
01:04:07,891 --> 01:04:10,393
In America, we just have a…
like a Snoopy balloon.

837
01:04:11,019 --> 01:04:12,687
Thanksgiving. So boring.

838
01:04:17,609 --> 01:04:20,028
Probably best to turn this off now.

839
01:04:22,739 --> 01:04:27,534
This is where Deputy Chairman
Dukhov's Altai phone was stolen.

840
01:04:27,535 --> 01:04:30,204
Just 90 kilometers south of here

841
01:04:30,205 --> 01:04:34,792
the railway
where our troops engaged with the targets.

842
01:04:34,793 --> 01:04:36,335
What time was the robbery?

843
01:04:36,336 --> 01:04:38,713
Approximately 2100 hours.

844
01:04:42,968 --> 01:04:47,597
Here. A call to the US Embassy at 2214
where monitoring was switched off.

845
01:04:48,181 --> 01:04:49,516
That must have been him.

846
01:04:59,609 --> 01:05:01,068
He is coming to us.

847
01:05:01,069 --> 01:05:03,112
I'll inform the general secretary.

848
01:05:03,113 --> 01:05:04,572
No.

849
01:05:04,573 --> 01:05:08,243
I want to greet
our American friend myself.

850
01:05:16,751 --> 01:05:18,253
This place is nice.

851
01:05:19,963 --> 01:05:21,298
Isn't nice.

852
01:05:33,685 --> 01:05:35,020
- What's that for?
- Follow me.

853
01:05:42,277 --> 01:05:43,277
You sure it's 709?

854
01:05:43,278 --> 01:05:44,821
It's 809. Come on, we'll take the stairs.

855
01:05:46,323 --> 01:05:47,616
Oh, come on.

856
01:05:49,576 --> 01:05:51,911
Hey, remember when you drove the car
onto the ice

857
01:05:51,912 --> 01:05:53,663
and then sank that car without warning me?

858
01:05:54,164 --> 01:05:55,540
Getting that same vibe here.

859
01:05:59,169 --> 01:06:00,170
Hello, Anna.

860
01:06:01,129 --> 01:06:02,672
Do you have a safe house we can use?

861
01:06:03,298 --> 01:06:04,216
Yes.

862
01:06:05,926 --> 01:06:06,927
Hi.

863
01:06:33,954 --> 01:06:35,537
All right, what is all this?

864
01:06:35,538 --> 01:06:38,832
There were four state security men
staking out the building.

865
01:06:38,833 --> 01:06:40,293
But they will not catch us.

866
01:06:44,506 --> 01:06:45,715
Eighth floor.

867
01:07:09,281 --> 01:07:10,782
Do you own or rent?

868
01:07:13,910 --> 01:07:15,161
Anna, come.

869
01:08:05,253 --> 01:08:06,670
I'm Troy, by the way.

870
01:08:06,671 --> 01:08:07,672
- Anna.
- Pleasure.

871
01:08:11,509 --> 01:08:13,010
So, first thing in the morning,

872
01:08:13,011 --> 01:08:15,054
Troy will call the embassy
on the Altai phone

873
01:08:15,055 --> 01:08:17,057
and the three of us
can leave here forever.

874
01:08:19,351 --> 01:08:21,186
Is this all true?
You're an Air Force pilot?

875
01:08:22,312 --> 01:08:23,812
No, Navy pilot.

876
01:08:23,813 --> 01:08:26,607
We have planes and boats.
It's confusing, I know.

877
01:08:28,360 --> 01:08:30,987
Do you know how long
it's been since we've spoken?

878
01:08:32,489 --> 01:08:34,198
Why would you think I'd go with you?

879
01:08:34,199 --> 01:08:36,450
It's a chance to start over.

880
01:08:36,451 --> 01:08:37,451
I'm not like you.

881
01:08:39,579 --> 01:08:42,081
I don't want to run off
to the woods and hide.

882
01:08:42,790 --> 01:08:44,874
I'd rather make the home I have better.

883
01:08:44,875 --> 01:08:46,585
You won't be safe if you stay.

884
01:08:47,420 --> 01:08:49,464
I've never been safe here.

885
01:08:50,757 --> 01:08:52,676
Go to the States if you can.

886
01:08:55,094 --> 01:08:58,097
You have many things to feel guilty about.

887
01:08:58,098 --> 01:09:00,350
But leaving me shouldn't be one of them.

888
01:09:06,481 --> 01:09:08,315
Does the stove work?

889
01:09:08,316 --> 01:09:10,484
What, are you gonna
blow this place up too?

890
01:09:10,485 --> 01:09:11,526
I'm making tea.

891
01:09:11,527 --> 01:09:12,987
Oh, I'll have some tea.

892
01:09:16,199 --> 01:09:18,326
You some kind of freedom fighter?

893
01:09:21,161 --> 01:09:23,956
The organization I'm in
works for human rights.

894
01:09:24,790 --> 01:09:25,875
They allow that here?

895
01:09:27,878 --> 01:09:29,962
They can only forbid what they know about.

896
01:09:29,963 --> 01:09:32,923
And they can only punish
the ones they catch.

897
01:09:32,924 --> 01:09:35,427
So they employ men like my father
to sniff us out.

898
01:09:37,846 --> 01:09:39,888
Did you do the stitching yourself?

899
01:09:39,889 --> 01:09:41,891
No. No, no, no, your dad did it.

900
01:09:41,892 --> 01:09:44,894
He's trained to create wounds,
not treat them.

901
01:09:44,895 --> 01:09:47,605
Appreciate you taking us in for the night.

902
01:09:47,606 --> 01:09:50,901
I didn't have much choice.
You led my father's comrades to my door.

903
01:09:51,817 --> 01:09:53,486
Well, ex-comrades.

904
01:09:55,238 --> 01:09:56,239
Yeah.

905
01:09:59,284 --> 01:10:01,328
I don't know what my father has told you,

906
01:10:02,746 --> 01:10:04,664
but I wouldn't put much trust in him.

907
01:10:05,540 --> 01:10:08,125
- Right.
- He lies for a living.

908
01:10:08,126 --> 01:10:09,835
I get that. But on the other hand,

909
01:10:09,836 --> 01:10:13,005
he's saved my life, like, 44 times
in the last couple of days,

910
01:10:13,006 --> 01:10:15,466
so I'm gonna give him
the benefit of the doubt.

911
01:10:15,467 --> 01:10:19,262
Yes. Well, I hope you make it home
safe to your family.

912
01:10:20,138 --> 01:10:21,932
No family, just my dad.

913
01:10:22,599 --> 01:10:26,143
Really?
A handsome American pilot like you?

914
01:10:26,144 --> 01:10:28,647
I assumed you had a wife and kids

915
01:10:29,564 --> 01:10:31,649
and a house with a picket fence.

916
01:10:31,650 --> 01:10:34,068
No. Single. Condo with a chain-link.

917
01:10:34,069 --> 01:10:36,571
I've been mostly focused on my work.

918
01:10:37,656 --> 01:10:40,075
Looks like that's really paying off.

919
01:10:40,825 --> 01:10:42,034
Thanks.

920
01:10:42,035 --> 01:10:44,621
What about you?
Is there a man in your life?

921
01:10:49,084 --> 01:10:50,085
Not my type.

922
01:10:50,669 --> 01:10:51,711
Come on, all men?

923
01:10:58,093 --> 01:11:02,429
I figure since I'm hiding you,
you can keep a secret.

924
01:11:02,430 --> 01:11:03,848
Does Nick know?

925
01:11:08,645 --> 01:11:11,231
It is against the law to be gay
in the Soviet Union.

926
01:11:11,731 --> 01:11:13,984
And that law is enforced by the KGB.

927
01:11:16,319 --> 01:11:17,320
Right.

928
01:11:23,827 --> 01:11:25,203
Anna's great, by the way.

929
01:11:26,830 --> 01:11:28,373
Much gentler touch than you.

930
01:11:29,124 --> 01:11:31,001
She's a very special girl.

931
01:11:32,794 --> 01:11:35,170
I wish things were different between us.

932
01:11:35,171 --> 01:11:36,715
Yeah, I bet she does too.

933
01:11:42,387 --> 01:11:44,139
Don't you…
Don't you see what you're doing?

934
01:11:45,724 --> 01:11:48,017
You're making the same mistakes
that Maverick did.

935
01:11:48,018 --> 01:11:49,184
Maverick from Top Gun?

936
01:11:49,185 --> 01:11:51,604
- Do you know another Maverick?
- Not really.

937
01:11:51,605 --> 01:11:52,688
After Goose died,

938
01:11:52,689 --> 01:11:56,400
Mav was wracked with guilt about all the
things that he could've done differently.

939
01:11:56,401 --> 01:12:00,530
All the things that he wished he could've
said to him. But it was too late.

940
01:12:01,948 --> 01:12:04,117
You still have a chance to talk to Anna.

941
01:12:05,160 --> 01:12:06,243
And who knows?

942
01:12:06,244 --> 01:12:10,497
You know, maybe you'll discover
stuff you didn't know about each other.

943
01:12:10,498 --> 01:12:11,582
What stuff?

944
01:12:11,583 --> 01:12:14,001
Yeah, well, private stuff.
You know, personal--

945
01:12:14,002 --> 01:12:15,754
You mean that she likes women?

946
01:12:16,838 --> 01:12:18,839
- Wait, you know?
- Yeah, I've always known.

947
01:12:18,840 --> 01:12:21,218
I mean, that's one of the reasons
why I left the KGB.

948
01:12:21,718 --> 01:12:24,763
How could I work for a system
that considered my own child a criminal?

949
01:12:25,597 --> 01:12:28,182
Why… Why didn't you talk to her about it?

950
01:12:28,183 --> 01:12:32,394
Look, if Anna wanted to discuss it,
she would come to me.

951
01:12:32,395 --> 01:12:33,729
That's not how it works.

952
01:12:33,730 --> 01:12:34,731
You're the dad.

953
01:12:35,357 --> 01:12:38,568
You need to show her that she
doesn't need to hide who she is from you.

954
01:12:41,821 --> 01:12:44,198
Are all fighter pilots
as sensitive as you?

955
01:12:44,199 --> 01:12:45,200
Yes.

956
01:12:50,830 --> 01:12:54,417
Can we talk?

957
01:12:56,836 --> 01:12:57,837
All right.

958
01:14:38,730 --> 01:14:41,565
DAD, CALL ME
WHEN YOU MAKE IT TO AMERICA.

959
01:14:41,566 --> 01:14:44,110
AND DON'T WORRY ABOUT ME.

960
01:14:49,074 --> 01:14:51,742
Our building
is typically surveilled by state security,

961
01:14:51,743 --> 01:14:54,286
so arrive at 9:00
and come straight to the gate.

962
01:14:54,287 --> 01:14:57,248
You'll debrief here and ship out
to Ramstein before end of day.

963
01:14:57,249 --> 01:14:58,832
Hooyah. Thank you, sir.

964
01:14:58,833 --> 01:15:00,417
Don't hang up yet, Lieutenant.

965
01:15:00,418 --> 01:15:02,003
I spoke with the ambassador.

966
01:15:03,088 --> 01:15:06,632
Unfortunately, we cannot
offer asylum to your civilian escort.

967
01:15:06,633 --> 01:15:08,635
Hold on. You don't understand.

968
01:15:09,135 --> 01:15:13,347
I wouldn't be here if not for Nick.
I promised I'd get him to the States.

969
01:15:13,348 --> 01:15:17,393
I hear you, but Nikolai Ustinov
is no ordinary citizen.

970
01:15:17,394 --> 01:15:18,978
Did you know he was KGB?

971
01:15:18,979 --> 01:15:21,272
Yeah. Yeah, he told me. But he quit.

972
01:15:21,273 --> 01:15:24,900
This is a very delicate moment
in US-Soviet relations.

973
01:15:24,901 --> 01:15:28,028
We give safe harbor to a KGB agent,
current or former--

974
01:15:28,029 --> 01:15:29,530
You gotta be kidding me.

975
01:15:29,531 --> 01:15:31,615
This guy is a major asset.

976
01:15:31,616 --> 01:15:34,076
A window into Soviet ops.
You should be jumping at this.

977
01:15:34,077 --> 01:15:37,079
My hands are tied.
This is coming from the highest level.

978
01:15:37,080 --> 01:15:39,082
Well, what am I supposed to tell the guy?

979
01:15:39,583 --> 01:15:42,127
He put his trust in me. In America.

980
01:15:42,961 --> 01:15:45,212
If I leave him behind,
we're no different than them.

981
01:15:45,213 --> 01:15:46,631
This is bullshit.

982
01:15:47,632 --> 01:15:50,010
I need confirmation
you'll be here at 9:00 this morning.

983
01:15:54,890 --> 01:15:55,891
I'll be there.

984
01:16:06,443 --> 01:16:07,652
It won't be long now.

985
01:16:10,447 --> 01:16:12,991
Listen, Nick, before we get there…

986
01:16:13,783 --> 01:16:17,369
I… When I talked to the Embassy,
I got some bad news and…

987
01:16:17,370 --> 01:16:20,582
Oh, is this… Is this a dead end? What--

988
01:16:26,546 --> 01:16:27,671
What is this?

989
01:16:27,672 --> 01:16:29,257
I thought we were friends.

990
01:16:30,383 --> 01:16:31,675
Nick, you ratted me out?

991
01:16:31,676 --> 01:16:34,179
You were leaving me
and my daughter to the wolves.

992
01:16:35,972 --> 01:16:37,891
Oh, come on, Nick. No, no, no, no, Nick.

993
01:16:39,809 --> 01:16:40,810
What did you do?

994
01:16:41,311 --> 01:16:44,272
Get off me! Hey! Hey, Nick!

995
01:17:04,668 --> 01:17:07,504
This was not our agreement!

996
01:17:14,427 --> 01:17:16,763
Get Volkov. This is unacceptable.

997
01:17:17,597 --> 01:17:18,682
Well, look who's here.

998
01:17:20,016 --> 01:17:21,809
Feeling pretty good about
making that call now?

999
01:17:21,810 --> 01:17:23,978
You lying bastard.
You promised you'd get me out of here.

1000
01:17:23,979 --> 01:17:26,605
I was gonna convince them
to take you in when we got to the Embassy.

1001
01:17:26,606 --> 01:17:29,149
More lies! Why didn't you tell me
they'd refused me asylum?

1002
01:17:29,150 --> 01:17:30,693
You never would've driven me there.

1003
01:17:30,694 --> 01:17:31,986
See? You're…

1004
01:17:31,987 --> 01:17:34,697
I swear to God
I was not gonna just leave you there.

1005
01:17:34,698 --> 01:17:36,241
I am… That is not who I am.

1006
01:17:37,075 --> 01:17:38,617
I don't know who you are.

1007
01:17:38,618 --> 01:17:41,371
Yes, you do. I'm a Top Gun.
I'm Maverick. You love me.

1008
01:17:42,747 --> 01:17:45,083
That is just a movie. I know that now.

1009
01:17:47,210 --> 01:17:48,169
Nick…

1010
01:17:51,089 --> 01:17:52,215
Gentlemen.

1011
01:17:53,091 --> 01:17:54,885
You lied. You said I'd be released.

1012
01:17:55,510 --> 01:17:58,388
And you will. One of you will.

1013
01:17:59,222 --> 01:18:00,974
- What is this?
- A confession.

1014
01:18:01,725 --> 01:18:03,643
It states that your objective here

1015
01:18:04,185 --> 01:18:07,564
was to infiltrate the Kremlin
and assassinate President Gorbachev.

1016
01:18:08,064 --> 01:18:11,067
And yours affirms
that he disclosed this mission to you.

1017
01:18:12,319 --> 01:18:13,736
Well, that's not true.

1018
01:18:13,737 --> 01:18:18,158
But if enough people believe it,
that will put an end to this Glasnost.

1019
01:18:19,659 --> 01:18:20,785
Openness.

1020
01:18:21,286 --> 01:18:24,706
The only thing we've opened ourselves to
is dissent and disorder.

1021
01:18:25,498 --> 01:18:28,418
Once you sign,
you'll be very well taken care of here.

1022
01:18:29,544 --> 01:18:33,422
A new identity with more
comfort and luxury than you can imagine.

1023
01:18:33,423 --> 01:18:38,093
You, sir, are an ugly man.
And that is an ugly suggestion.

1024
01:18:38,094 --> 01:18:41,430
Your country refused to extract you
from behind enemy lines,

1025
01:18:41,431 --> 01:18:44,226
- leaving you to fend for yourself.
- I know what I signed up for.

1026
01:18:45,602 --> 01:18:46,770
How about your father?

1027
01:18:48,188 --> 01:18:52,484
Did he know his government was killing him
and taking no responsibility?

1028
01:18:53,235 --> 01:18:54,777
What did you say?

1029
01:18:54,778 --> 01:18:56,363
We do our research.

1030
01:18:59,699 --> 01:19:00,992
Harold Kelly.

1031
01:19:01,660 --> 01:19:05,454
Diagnosed in 1983
with malignant pleural mesothelioma.

1032
01:19:05,455 --> 01:19:08,332
Worked for 32 years
at the San Diego shipyards

1033
01:19:08,333 --> 01:19:12,711
where he was exposed to high levels of
asbestos on a daily basis.

1034
01:19:12,712 --> 01:19:14,129
Why is this America's fault?

1035
01:19:14,130 --> 01:19:17,341
They knew the dangers, but suppressed
that information for decades

1036
01:19:17,342 --> 01:19:18,468
because it saved them money.

1037
01:19:19,052 --> 01:19:20,053
How would you know that?

1038
01:19:21,221 --> 01:19:24,473
This is a copy of the classified letter
from your Secretary of the Navy

1039
01:19:24,474 --> 01:19:27,017
dated September 1956.

1040
01:19:27,018 --> 01:19:28,895
I told you we do our research.

1041
01:19:30,105 --> 01:19:31,648
Nations are like people.

1042
01:19:32,941 --> 01:19:35,902
They do what they must to survive.

1043
01:19:36,778 --> 01:19:39,656
The only question is, will you?

1044
01:19:44,286 --> 01:19:45,287
I…

1045
01:19:46,621 --> 01:19:50,292
Before I came here, I…
I thought I knew what this country was.

1046
01:19:50,917 --> 01:19:52,919
But there's something I didn't know.

1047
01:19:53,837 --> 01:19:56,423
I didn't know that
there were good people here.

1048
01:19:57,257 --> 01:20:00,302
People who will risk their lives
to help a stranger.

1049
01:20:02,095 --> 01:20:04,931
So, no, I won't… I won't sign that.

1050
01:20:06,391 --> 01:20:09,394
Not for the sake of my country.
But for the sake of yours.

1051
01:20:12,439 --> 01:20:13,689
And you, comrade?

1052
01:20:13,690 --> 01:20:16,526
You've proven your loyalty
by turning him in.

1053
01:20:17,193 --> 01:20:20,447
Are you willing to take the final step
for your country?

1054
01:20:23,199 --> 01:20:24,659
For your family?

1055
01:20:30,832 --> 01:20:32,167
What is loyalty?

1056
01:20:32,834 --> 01:20:34,543
An exercise for fools.

1057
01:20:34,544 --> 01:20:36,671
America. Russia. It's all shit.

1058
01:20:37,464 --> 01:20:39,132
None of us escape what we are.

1059
01:20:40,508 --> 01:20:43,344
If it will protect me and my family,
I'll sign your paper.

1060
01:20:43,345 --> 01:20:44,346
Nick.

1061
01:20:45,138 --> 01:20:46,890
What difference does it make?

1062
01:20:47,641 --> 01:20:48,475
Very good.

1063
01:20:50,477 --> 01:20:52,479
Your KGB training taught you well.

1064
01:20:53,271 --> 01:20:58,109
My training also taught me
never to give a prisoner a sharp object.

1065
01:21:00,737 --> 01:21:02,655
Goddamn it. I knew it was an act.

1066
01:21:02,656 --> 01:21:04,907
- You did?
- No, but thank God.

1067
01:21:04,908 --> 01:21:07,701
- I still have not forgiven you.
- Same. Why do we need that?

1068
01:21:07,702 --> 01:21:10,205
If we survive,
this will make sure he does not.

1069
01:21:12,374 --> 01:21:14,167
- You ready for this?
- No.

1070
01:21:23,009 --> 01:21:24,176
Where are we?

1071
01:21:24,177 --> 01:21:28,722
KGB black site.
Used for less formal interrogations.

1072
01:21:28,723 --> 01:21:30,141
So Volkov was going rogue?

1073
01:21:30,934 --> 01:21:34,020
Some men have their own agendas.
But you would know that.

1074
01:21:34,854 --> 01:21:36,565
You're the one who
called the torture police.

1075
01:21:42,320 --> 01:21:43,321
Hey!

1076
01:21:58,712 --> 01:22:01,798
Stop! Stop!

1077
01:22:20,567 --> 01:22:23,319
- Do we go back to the Embassy?
- KGB will be swarming the area.

1078
01:22:23,320 --> 01:22:25,529
We need to leave the country.
Where's the nearest airport?

1079
01:22:25,530 --> 01:22:27,531
Sheremetyevo.
It's about 12 kilometers from here.

1080
01:22:27,532 --> 01:22:30,284
Okay, okay.
All right, well, we need a car.

1081
01:22:30,285 --> 01:22:32,412
A car they can stop.
We need something bigger.

1082
01:22:34,623 --> 01:22:36,665
- You wanna steal a tank?
- A tank they can shoot at.

1083
01:22:36,666 --> 01:22:38,335
They can shoot at anything.

1084
01:22:40,962 --> 01:22:41,963
Not anything.

1085
01:22:45,634 --> 01:22:46,717
No.

1086
01:22:46,718 --> 01:22:49,387
I doubt they'll shoot
at a nuclear missile.

1087
01:22:50,347 --> 01:22:52,015
- You doubt?
- Hey!

1088
01:23:14,996 --> 01:23:17,706
- What did you say to him?
- That he had driven over my baby.

1089
01:23:17,707 --> 01:23:21,169
That just popped into your head?
What is it with you and babies?

1090
01:23:23,255 --> 01:23:24,256
Hey!

1091
01:23:36,226 --> 01:23:37,352
Oh, God.

1092
01:23:42,399 --> 01:23:44,233
Get out of the car!

1093
01:23:44,234 --> 01:23:48,320
I want every unit in pursuit of
that mobile launcher.

1094
01:23:48,321 --> 01:23:50,490
No one is to fire on them!

1095
01:24:08,133 --> 01:24:10,385
- You're seeing this, right?
- I'm seeing it.

1096
01:24:38,622 --> 01:24:40,040
Bus, bus, bus, bus, bus, bus!

1097
01:25:12,155 --> 01:25:13,906
Maybe we should clear the air.

1098
01:25:13,907 --> 01:25:15,491
What is there to clear, Troy?

1099
01:25:15,492 --> 01:25:18,077
I risk everything to save you
and you pissed on my back.

1100
01:25:18,078 --> 01:25:21,873
Oh, that's funny 'cause I seem to
remember your piss running down my back.

1101
01:25:22,540 --> 01:25:26,126
I asked for asylum for you, they said no,
you threw me in a dungeon.

1102
01:25:26,127 --> 01:25:28,337
You promised
your country would protect us.

1103
01:25:28,338 --> 01:25:31,340
Well, it turns out that
my country isn't perfect.

1104
01:25:31,341 --> 01:25:34,094
My dad meant nothing to them
and neither do you or I.

1105
01:25:44,437 --> 01:25:45,730
Well, look, if I'm being…

1106
01:25:46,523 --> 01:25:48,608
if I'm being totally honest with myself,

1107
01:25:49,401 --> 01:25:51,278
maybe I was
just thinking about getting home.

1108
01:25:54,155 --> 01:25:56,116
Maybe I'm kind of a selfish guy.

1109
01:26:02,330 --> 01:26:05,292
The least I could've done was tell you
'cause you're my friend.

1110
01:26:06,376 --> 01:26:07,836
And that's what friends do.

1111
01:26:11,631 --> 01:26:12,841
Move.

1112
01:26:42,537 --> 01:26:44,789
Fine, you wanna know
why they call me Assassin?

1113
01:26:47,375 --> 01:26:50,502
Back when I was a JG,
I made my first carrier landing

1114
01:26:50,503 --> 01:26:51,504
and I was…

1115
01:26:52,380 --> 01:26:54,591
I was feeling pretty proud of myself.

1116
01:26:55,217 --> 01:26:56,635
So I get out of the plane,

1117
01:26:57,135 --> 01:26:59,095
I wasn't looking where I was going,

1118
01:27:00,430 --> 01:27:02,849
and I fell ass-first into a deck hatch.

1119
01:27:03,975 --> 01:27:05,643
A couple green shirts, they helped me up.

1120
01:27:05,644 --> 01:27:08,104
I look around to see
if anyone else noticed and I…

1121
01:27:09,606 --> 01:27:10,982
Shit, I did it again.

1122
01:27:12,192 --> 01:27:14,444
I fell ass-first into the same hatch.

1123
01:27:15,403 --> 01:27:16,529
I don't understand.

1124
01:27:17,030 --> 01:27:19,366
I fell, ass in.

1125
01:27:20,283 --> 01:27:21,785
Twice. Get it?

1126
01:27:22,369 --> 01:27:24,120
Ass, ass, in.

1127
01:27:27,791 --> 01:27:29,124
That is embarrassing.

1128
01:27:29,125 --> 01:27:33,338
Point is, I've never told
anyone outside the service that story.

1129
01:27:34,506 --> 01:27:36,550
But I'm telling you now as a gesture.

1130
01:27:38,093 --> 01:27:39,510
A gesture?

1131
01:27:39,511 --> 01:27:40,887
Of trust.

1132
01:27:42,639 --> 01:27:45,600
You're trusting that I will tell no one
that you disgraced yourself?

1133
01:27:46,810 --> 01:27:47,811
Yes.

1134
01:27:54,568 --> 01:27:56,193
Trying to pull another lever?

1135
01:27:56,194 --> 01:27:58,321
I appreciate you telling me your secret,

1136
01:27:58,989 --> 01:28:00,115
Ass-ass-in.

1137
01:28:03,743 --> 01:28:05,328
You can just run it together.

1138
01:28:07,289 --> 01:28:08,747
Ass-ass-in.

1139
01:28:08,748 --> 01:28:09,874
Assassin.

1140
01:28:10,458 --> 01:28:12,127
Our bomb's not gonna clear that.

1141
01:29:00,550 --> 01:29:03,636
- Where are the private jets?
- Private planes leave from Vnukovo.

1142
01:29:03,637 --> 01:29:04,721
Where's that?

1143
01:29:05,347 --> 01:29:06,765
An hour away.

1144
01:29:09,100 --> 01:29:10,852
Then I guess we're flying commercial.

1145
01:29:18,944 --> 01:29:22,155
My baby's in there!
My baby's in there!

1146
01:29:26,785 --> 01:29:28,452
Oh, God!

1147
01:29:28,453 --> 01:29:29,912
God!

1148
01:29:29,913 --> 01:29:30,829
Follow me!

1149
01:29:30,830 --> 01:29:32,957
- Why did you do that?
- What do you mean?

1150
01:29:32,958 --> 01:29:35,459
- I took a bullet for you.
- You didn't take it.

1151
01:29:35,460 --> 01:29:38,546
You shared it.
You can't stop a bullet with your hand.

1152
01:29:38,547 --> 01:29:40,632
I know that now. And I knew that then.

1153
01:29:52,978 --> 01:29:54,938
Pull up close to the cabin door!

1154
01:29:57,816 --> 01:29:58,817
Closer!

1155
01:29:59,734 --> 01:30:01,152
You wanna get the door, please?

1156
01:30:18,753 --> 01:30:20,463
What are they paying this guy?

1157
01:30:38,940 --> 01:30:39,774
Hey!

1158
01:31:38,625 --> 01:31:39,793
Once you are dead,

1159
01:31:40,460 --> 01:31:42,378
I will hunt down your daughter

1160
01:31:42,379 --> 01:31:43,838
and kill her too!

1161
01:31:47,342 --> 01:31:49,469
You are a traitor and a fool!

1162
01:31:55,141 --> 01:31:56,767
No, Volkov.

1163
01:31:56,768 --> 01:31:58,770
I must break you.

1164
01:31:59,396 --> 01:32:00,814
Is that what he said?

1165
01:32:09,281 --> 01:32:11,115
I don't think that killed him.

1166
01:32:11,116 --> 01:32:12,908
Who is flying the plane?

1167
01:32:12,909 --> 01:32:14,578
I put it on autopilot.

1168
01:32:15,662 --> 01:32:17,080
I put it on something.

1169
01:32:24,754 --> 01:32:26,256
How far until Finland?

1170
01:32:26,882 --> 01:32:27,883
Too far.

1171
01:32:28,550 --> 01:32:30,509
When we lost that engine,
we lost our airspeed.

1172
01:32:30,510 --> 01:32:33,095
We won't make it to Finland.
We don't have the fuel.

1173
01:32:33,096 --> 01:32:36,016
- Where does that leave us?
- Somewhere over the Baltic Sea.

1174
01:32:37,684 --> 01:32:39,560
Or if we can find Carl Vinson.

1175
01:32:39,561 --> 01:32:41,520
Who is this man, Vinson?
How can he help us?

1176
01:32:41,521 --> 01:32:43,398
He's not a man. He was a man.

1177
01:32:44,065 --> 01:32:45,399
Now he's an aircraft carrier.

1178
01:32:45,400 --> 01:32:47,193
Can a plane this size land on a carrier?

1179
01:32:48,028 --> 01:32:49,905
Technically, no. But physically,

1180
01:32:50,614 --> 01:32:51,615
probably not.

1181
01:32:55,035 --> 01:32:59,163
Captain, TAO.
Unidentified aircraft, course 110,

1182
01:32:59,164 --> 01:33:00,664
20 miles, 5,000 feet.

1183
01:33:00,665 --> 01:33:02,207
- Military?
- No, sir.

1184
01:33:02,208 --> 01:33:04,627
- It's squawking commercial air.
- All right, hail them on guard.

1185
01:33:04,628 --> 01:33:07,171
Unidentified aircraft, course 285,

1186
01:33:07,172 --> 01:33:10,049
you are approaching a US warship
operating in international waters.

1187
01:33:10,050 --> 01:33:12,134
Request you identify yourself
and state intentions.

1188
01:33:12,135 --> 01:33:15,304
This is Lieutenant Troy Kelly
of the United States Navy.

1189
01:33:15,305 --> 01:33:19,225
We are declaring an emergency
and requesting a ready deck upon arrival.

1190
01:33:19,226 --> 01:33:22,394
Unidentified aircraft,
alter course immediately or you

1191
01:33:22,395 --> 01:33:24,021
may be subject to defensive measures.

1192
01:33:24,022 --> 01:33:25,105
- Holy shit.
- What?

1193
01:33:25,106 --> 01:33:27,484
Okay, we can hear them
but they can't hear us.

1194
01:33:28,652 --> 01:33:31,237
Let's get a visual. Launch the alert five.

1195
01:33:31,238 --> 01:33:34,156
If we can't communicate with them,
they're gonna assume that we're hostile,

1196
01:33:34,157 --> 01:33:35,532
and they're gonna run an intercept on us.

1197
01:33:35,533 --> 01:33:38,953
No, I can fix this. How long do we have?

1198
01:33:38,954 --> 01:33:40,956
As long as you need,
until we're shot down.

1199
01:33:48,755 --> 01:33:51,757
Skopa Air, alter course
immediately and acknowledge.

1200
01:33:51,758 --> 01:33:54,594
- How is that coming?
- It is trickier than my ham radio.

1201
01:33:55,470 --> 01:33:57,805
Captain, that was an alert from Interpol.

1202
01:33:57,806 --> 01:34:01,392
Commercial ATR 42 was seized by gunmen
at Sheremetyevo an hour ago.

1203
01:34:01,393 --> 01:34:04,437
TAO, set weapons posture one, all mounts.

1204
01:34:16,366 --> 01:34:18,200
- They're detaching.
- That's good.

1205
01:34:18,201 --> 01:34:20,036
That's bad.
They're getting out of the way.

1206
01:34:25,250 --> 01:34:27,585
Designating track 141 hostile.

1207
01:34:27,586 --> 01:34:28,627
All mounts in remote.

1208
01:34:28,628 --> 01:34:29,962
Awaiting batteries release.

1209
01:34:29,963 --> 01:34:32,923
- Permission grant--
- Repeat, this is Lieutenant Troy Kelly…

1210
01:34:32,924 --> 01:34:36,261
- Belay that.
- 7741. I've been MIA. Do you copy?

1211
01:34:40,140 --> 01:34:41,266
Welcome back, Lieutenant.

1212
01:34:43,643 --> 01:34:45,603
Mayday! Mayday! Mayday!

1213
01:34:45,604 --> 01:34:48,523
We're below minimum fuel.
Request emergency landing. Over.

1214
01:34:49,107 --> 01:34:50,900
In that thing? Without a tailhook?

1215
01:34:50,901 --> 01:34:52,276
He's nuts.

1216
01:34:52,277 --> 01:34:54,445
What's the wingspan on the ATR-42?

1217
01:34:54,446 --> 01:34:55,447
Eighty-one feet, sir.

1218
01:34:56,197 --> 01:34:58,533
It's tight, but it's possible.

1219
01:35:00,285 --> 01:35:01,368
This is the captain.

1220
01:35:01,369 --> 01:35:04,204
On the flight deck,
emergency pull-forward.

1221
01:35:04,205 --> 01:35:05,749
All ahead full.

1222
01:35:09,836 --> 01:35:12,464
Skopa Air 1628, you are clear for landing.

1223
01:35:14,382 --> 01:35:16,343
Congratulations, Troy.

1224
01:35:18,261 --> 01:35:19,930
You're going home.

1225
01:35:21,223 --> 01:35:22,641
Yes, I am.

1226
01:35:36,696 --> 01:35:39,199
Captain, I need you to help me
with something before I can land.

1227
01:35:39,741 --> 01:35:40,658
Name it.

1228
01:35:40,659 --> 01:35:45,955
I need permanent asylum status
for a Soviet citizen, Nikolai Ustinov.

1229
01:35:45,956 --> 01:35:46,872
What?

1230
01:35:46,873 --> 01:35:49,124
I'm not authorized to grant that.

1231
01:35:49,125 --> 01:35:52,086
Then I think you should ask
somebody at the State Department who can,

1232
01:35:52,087 --> 01:35:53,337
because you hear this?

1233
01:35:53,338 --> 01:35:55,548
We're down to 20 kilos of fuel.

1234
01:35:55,549 --> 01:35:58,008
I don't understand.
You've been given permission to land.

1235
01:35:58,009 --> 01:36:01,887
And I respectfully decline permission
to land until I get what I'm asking.

1236
01:36:01,888 --> 01:36:03,180
Fifteen kilos.

1237
01:36:03,181 --> 01:36:04,598
This guy's a soup sandwich.

1238
01:36:04,599 --> 01:36:06,100
He's also an American MIA.

1239
01:36:06,101 --> 01:36:08,394
Get Assistant Director Meadows
on the horn.

1240
01:36:08,395 --> 01:36:09,229
Quickly.

1241
01:36:10,564 --> 01:36:12,314
Why are you doing this?

1242
01:36:12,315 --> 01:36:16,111
'Cause right now the only way to stand up
for my country is to stand up to it.

1243
01:36:20,240 --> 01:36:21,533
Thank you.

1244
01:36:25,870 --> 01:36:27,581
We're dead-stick, Captain.

1245
01:36:37,716 --> 01:36:40,885
Kelly, this is Karen Meadows
at the State Department.

1246
01:36:40,886 --> 01:36:44,013
Consul General Hennessy
has apprised me of your situation.

1247
01:36:44,014 --> 01:36:46,891
You should know
I don't like to have my arm twisted,

1248
01:36:46,892 --> 01:36:49,143
especially at 5:00 in the morning.

1249
01:36:49,144 --> 01:36:50,686
Understood, ma'am. Sorry to wake you.

1250
01:36:50,687 --> 01:36:52,521
But considering the circumstances,

1251
01:36:52,522 --> 01:36:55,483
I am officially granting
your request for asylum.

1252
01:36:56,109 --> 01:36:58,653
And I wanna thank you
for your service, Lieutenant.

1253
01:36:59,654 --> 01:37:01,698
Now, land the goddamn plane.

1254
01:37:03,575 --> 01:37:05,035
You risked your life for me.

1255
01:37:06,077 --> 01:37:08,622
Sort of. There's a reserve fuel tank.

1256
01:37:29,100 --> 01:37:30,517
Flaps 30.

1257
01:37:30,518 --> 01:37:33,438
Condition levers max. On-slope, on center.

1258
01:37:33,980 --> 01:37:36,691
It's like I'm inside my favorite movie.

1259
01:38:10,141 --> 01:38:11,935
- Hey, Troy.
- Yeah?

1260
01:38:12,936 --> 01:38:14,937
You can be my wingman any--

1261
01:38:14,938 --> 01:38:16,690
No. No, no, no. What is that? No.

1262
01:38:17,190 --> 01:38:18,483
No. We're not gonna do that.

1263
01:38:19,067 --> 01:38:20,193
I understand.

1264
01:38:27,742 --> 01:38:30,412
It's been my great honor
to serve this nation

1265
01:38:31,413 --> 01:38:35,500
and uphold the Navy's motto,
non sibi sed patriae.

1266
01:38:37,043 --> 01:38:38,712
"Not for self but for country."

1267
01:38:40,463 --> 01:38:42,047
Which is why I have the utmost confidence

1268
01:38:42,048 --> 01:38:44,800
that this body will issue
a public acknowledgement

1269
01:38:44,801 --> 01:38:49,097
of the government's use of cancer-causing
materials in military construction.

1270
01:38:55,604 --> 01:38:59,273
Additionally, I'd ask for the
establishment of a compensation committee

1271
01:38:59,274 --> 01:39:01,693
to reimburse the good people,
including my father,

1272
01:39:02,277 --> 01:39:05,405
who sacrificed their own well-being
to safeguard ours.

1273
01:39:08,658 --> 01:39:09,867
Thank you, Lieutenant.

1274
01:39:09,868 --> 01:39:12,244
This country owes you a debt of gratitude

1275
01:39:12,245 --> 01:39:14,873
and we will take your request
under serious advisement.

1276
01:39:18,501 --> 01:39:19,627
Sorry.

1277
01:39:19,628 --> 01:39:22,838
It's a little trick I picked up
from the Russian boy scouts.

1278
01:39:22,839 --> 01:39:25,550
I probably should've mentioned
that I have this.

1279
01:39:26,301 --> 01:39:28,302
This is a copy of a classified letter

1280
01:39:28,303 --> 01:39:30,888
sent from
the Secretary of the Navy in 1956

1281
01:39:30,889 --> 01:39:35,894
recognizing the health risks
posed by asbestos to shipyard workers.

1282
01:39:37,020 --> 01:39:39,647
I have the original somewhere. I just
can't quite remember where I put it.

1283
01:39:39,648 --> 01:39:42,234
This is just very damning though.
Very, very damning.

1284
01:39:43,860 --> 01:39:44,986
Bravo.

1285
01:39:50,033 --> 01:39:52,911
Well? How's the Big Mac?
Is it everything you hoped?

1286
01:39:53,536 --> 01:39:56,830
It tastes like America.

1287
01:39:56,831 --> 01:39:59,291
Huh. When do you head out?

1288
01:39:59,292 --> 01:40:00,209
At dawn.

1289
01:40:00,210 --> 01:40:02,503
I want to have lunch at the Liberty Bell.

1290
01:40:02,504 --> 01:40:04,380
Well, that's everyone's dream.

1291
01:40:04,381 --> 01:40:05,464
It's a beaut.

1292
01:40:05,465 --> 01:40:06,633
It is.

1293
01:40:07,801 --> 01:40:10,554
Didn't you say that
you had months of leave saved up?

1294
01:40:11,179 --> 01:40:14,431
After my little stunt, they may
put me on permanent leave.

1295
01:40:14,432 --> 01:40:16,559
So, why don't you join me?

1296
01:40:16,560 --> 01:40:18,936
You know, the kitchen table
folds down into a second bed.

1297
01:40:18,937 --> 01:40:21,939
There's a car phone,
so I can keep in touch with Anna.

1298
01:40:21,940 --> 01:40:23,399
I have a cassette player.

1299
01:40:23,400 --> 01:40:25,484
- I'm out.
- Understood.

1300
01:40:25,485 --> 01:40:27,361
But isn't it time
that you explored the country

1301
01:40:27,362 --> 01:40:29,197
that you fought so hard to protect?

1302
01:40:31,950 --> 01:40:33,242
I don't know.

1303
01:40:33,243 --> 01:40:35,954
Come on, Lieutenant.

1304
01:40:38,039 --> 01:40:39,457
One more adventure.

1305
01:40:42,252 --> 01:40:44,337
Let me finish my drink before I decide.

1306
01:40:44,921 --> 01:40:45,964
Of course.

